**Doctor:** Hi, Mr. [Patient's Name]. I'm Dr. [Doctor's Name]. I understand you've been experiencing some right elbow pain. Can you tell me more about what happened?

**Patient:** Yeah, my son was playing lacrosse and accidentally hit me with the stick. I've been having a lot of pain and swelling in my elbow since then.

**Doctor:** I see. And have you noticed any other symptoms besides the pain and swelling? Any difficulty moving your arm or numbness or tingling?

**Patient:** No, just the pain. But it's been getting worse over the past few days.

**Doctor:** Okay. I'd like to take a look at your elbow. (examines the patient's elbow) Can you flex and extend your arm for me? (patient demonstrates range of motion) And can you tell me where exactly the pain is?

**Patient:** It's right here (points to olecranon area).

**Doctor:** Okay. I'm going to take a look at your elbow again. (examines the patient's elbow) Yes, I can see some swelling and bruising. I'm going to order an X-ray to rule out any fractures or bony abnormalities.

**Patient:** Okay.

**Doctor:** The X-ray results came back normal, so it looks like you have a contusion, or a bruise, in your elbow. I'm going to prescribe some ibuprofen to help with the pain and swelling. I also want you to ice the area for 20 minutes, three times a day, to reduce the swelling.

**Patient:** Okay, that sounds good.

**Doctor:** Additionally, I want you to avoid playing lacrosse for the next couple of weeks to give your elbow time to heal. After that, you should be fine to continue playing normally.

**Patient:** Alright.

**Doctor:** I also want to check in with you about your blood pressure and blood sugar levels. Your blood pressure is a bit elevated, but it seems to be well-controlled with your current medications. We'll keep an eye on it. And your blood sugar levels seem to be under control with your current medication.

**Patient:** That's good to know.

**Doctor:** Just to recap, I've prescribed ibuprofen to help with the pain and swelling. I've also recommended avoiding lacrosse for the next couple of weeks. And we'll keep an eye on your blood pressure and blood sugar levels. If you have any further questions or concerns, don't hesitate to reach out to my office.

**Patient:** Alright, thank you.<|eot_id|>
