dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn, how are you?
[patient] hi, i'm okay. how are you?
[doctor] good. i'm doing well. i know you're here to follow up on some of your chronic problems. i know you were having some osteoarthritis and some gout, and some psoriasis. tell me a little bit about how you're doing with those.
[patient] yeah, my osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little bit lately, and i was wondering if we could talk about that. i've been sitting at the computer a lot more in the office, so i'm not sure if it's just from sitting in that position all day. it's mostly in my elbows.
[doctor] okay. so, it's both elbows, or is one more bothersome than the other?
[patient] my right elbow bothers me a little bit more than my left elbow, but i'm mostly typing all day versus writing, so i'm not writing as much.
[doctor] okay. all right. and any other joint pain?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and then i know you have a history of gout. how have you been doing with that?
[patient] yeah, i had an episode about three months ago, and it was in my toe. i had some inflammation in my toe at that time. i have not had any other issues with that since. the medicine they gave me helped, and i have not seen a flare up since.
[doctor] okay. and are you still on the colchicine?
[patient] yes, i am. i'm taking 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups of my gout.
[doctor] okay. and how about your psoriasis? how's that been?
[patient] it's under control. it really has not been a major problem for me.
[doctor] okay. and you're still on the steroid cream?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let me do a quick physical exam. your neck is nice and supple without any lymphadenopathy. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. your heart is a regular rate and rhythm. your abdomen is soft. i don't see any edema in your lower extremities. and when i examine your right elbow, there is some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. there is some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. there is some pain with pronation and supination. there is pain with flexion and extension of your right arm. so i'm gon na order an x-ray of your right elbow just to check for any arthritis in your joint.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and for the pain and swelling, i'm gon na prescribe you some meloxicam 15 mg once a day. it should help with the pain and the swelling. and continue with the colchicine that you're taking for your gout. and continue with the steroid cream for your psoriasis. does that sound good?
[patient] yes, that sounds good. thank you.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, take care.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
