dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi anna, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay.
[doctor] okay. i know you're here for some joint pain. can you tell me a little bit about what's going on with that?
[patient] sure. so i've been having a lot of pain in my left elbow. i sit at my desk all day at work and it's really bent. after i get out of work, it's really hard for me to flex and extend my elbow. it's been really stiff and painful.
[doctor] okay. and you said you sit at a desk all day at work. do you type a lot?
[patient] i do.
[doctor] okay. do you use a mouse?
[patient] yeah, i do.
[doctor] okay. and are you right-handed?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. that's good. so that means you can still write, which is great, but typing is difficult?
[patient] yeah, exactly.
[doctor] okay. any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. any weakness in your arm?
[patient] a little bit, but not too much.
[doctor] okay. any fever or chills?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. all right. let's talk a little bit about your past medical history. you have a history of epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. can you tell me a little bit about how you're doing with those?
[patient] sure. so, my epilepsy, i haven't had any recent seizures. my last seizure was a year ago. i'm still taking keppra, and i'm doing pretty well with that.
[doctor] okay. good to hear. and how about your depression? how are you doing with that?
[patient] so, i started therapy last year. i'm trying to avoid medications for it. i'm trying to do it all with therapy. it's been helpful, but i still feel down and stressed.
[doctor] okay. and any suicidal or homicidal ideations?
[patient] no, none of that.
[doctor] okay. all right. and how about your peptic ulcer disease? how are you doing with that?
[patient] so, last year, i was dealing with a lot of stress. i had an endoscopy and it showed that i had an episode of gastritis. they diagnosed me with peptic ulcer disease and started me on protonix. since then, i've not had any issues with it. everything's been good.
[doctor] okay. all right. any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?
[patient] no, nothing like that. i do have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm just gon na check out your elbow. hey, dragon, show me the exam. all right, so on physical exam, there is some erythema and edema of the left elbow. there is pain to palpation of the left olecranon. it's warm to palpation, and there is pain with flexion and extension. there is a palpable left radial pulse. so, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. i think you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. i'm gon na start you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you can also ice the area. you can take an ibuprofen or tylenol for pain. i'm gon na go ahead and refill your keppra. you can continue to take that 500 milligrams twice a day. and i'm gon na start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once a day for your depression. and then for your peptic ulcer disease, continue the protonix 40 milligrams once a day before meals. hey, dragon, order meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day. order lexapro 10 milligrams once a day. order protonix 40 milligrams once a day before meals. refill keppra 500 milligrams twice a day. all right, so, any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] all right. hey, dragon, finalize the note. }}<|eot_id|>
