dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, jordan. how are you?
[patient] good. how are you?
[doctor] good. so i know that you had a visit with the nurse practitioner in march, and she had ordered some blood work for you, and we're still waiting on those results. so i know that you had a problem with some palpitations and your blood pressure was high. do you remember what happened?
[patient] yeah. i had a panic attack.
[doctor] okay. so, do you still have any palpitations?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. and how's your blood pressure? have you been checking it at home?
[patient] yeah. it's been running between 146 and 155.
[doctor] okay. and what do you think might be causing that?
[patient] i don't know. i've been trying to watch my salt intake, but i think i'm still eating too much salt. i've been watching my diet.
[doctor] okay. so, have you been taking the benicar?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with that? are you taking it?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any difference with your blood pressure?
[patient] not really. it's been pretty consistent.
[doctor] okay. and have you been exercising?
[patient] i try to walk on the treadmill as much as i can.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel like you're watching your salt intake?
[patient] yeah, i'm doing pretty well with that.
[doctor] okay. so, we're gon na talk a little bit about your family history. you do have a family history of hypertension?
[patient] yes, several family members.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, i know that you have a new primary care physician, and they started you on benicar hct. have you been taking that?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with that?
[patient] it's been fine.
[doctor] okay. and i know that you're on the amlodipine, 10 milligrams a day, right?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na take your vital signs. your blood pressure today is 140 over 80, so that's good. your heart rate is normal, and your lungs are clear to auscultation. your abdomen is non-tender. you don't have any edema. so, let's talk a little bit about your thyroid profile. it was normal, correct?
[patient] yes, it was.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, i know that we're still waiting on your lab results, but i'm gon na go ahead and order a few more tests. i want to see if your blood pressure is resistant to the medication that you're on, and we're gon na do a basic metabolic panel to check your electrolytes. so, i'm gon na order some labs and we'll go from there.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, your blood pressure is resistant to the medication that you're on. we have to consider adding another medication to help lower it. and the one that i would like to start you on is spironolactone. have you ever heard of that?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. it's a medication that helps lower blood pressure, and it's very effective, but it can have some side effects. it can cause gynecomastia, which is the growth of breast tissue in men, and it can also cause electrolyte disturbances. so, we'll need to monitor your potassium and sodium levels.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and we'll also have to watch for dizziness, because you can be dehydrated.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, i know that you're already watching your salt intake, and that's a good thing. i would like you to try to get your sodium intake to 1500 to less than 2000 milligrams a day. have you seen the dash diet?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. so, i'll give you some information about that. it's a diet that can help lower your blood pressure, and it's very low in salt. i also want you to try to walk at least 30 minutes a day. so, i'd like you to meet with me in two weeks, and we'll check your blood pressure and we'll check your electrolytes. and if you're not doing well with the spironolactone, we may need to send you to the resistant hypertension clinic.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] all right. well, take care. i'll see you in two weeks.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
