[patient] no fever.
[doctor] okay. any bleeding from your nose or gums?
[patient] no, no bleeding from my gums.
[doctor] okay. any shortness of breath, any hemoptysis, like you said, any other symptoms?
[patient] yeah, just shortness of breath and the hemoptysis.
[doctor] okay. any lower extremity edema, knee pain?
[patient] yeah, i do have some knee pain. but no swelling in my legs.
[doctor] okay. and any bruising?
[patient] no bruising.
[doctor] okay. all right. let's go ahead and look at your vitals. your pulse oxygenation is 94 percent. your blood pressure is 120 over 70. those are good numbers. let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'll start with your neck. your neck is nice and supple. no jugular venous distention. no carotid bruits. good. let's listen to your lungs. i do hear some rales and rhonchi, more on the right. no wheezing right now. there is some diminished breath sounds in the right as well. let's listen to your heart. your heart has a regular rate. i do appreciate a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur, unchanged from before. let's examine your abdomen. your abdomen is nice and soft. and on your lower extremities, i do appreciate 1+ nonpitting edema on both the bilateral lower extremities. no calf tenderness. and on your skin exam, no bruising. all right, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. for your first problem, your shortness of breath with hemoptysis, this could be something as simple as a pneumonia, but it could be something more serious. i'd like to get a chest x-ray, a ct scan, and some blood work done in the er. i'll go ahead and call ahead and let them know that you're coming in. i want you to go into the er right after this appointment. i'd like to get these tests done as soon as possible. for your second problem, your diabetes, your blood sugar has not been well controlled. i'd like to get an updated a1c today. i'm going to increase your metformin to 750 milligrams twice daily. for your third problem, your hypertension, your blood pressure has been running low for about three weeks. i believe this could be caused by your shortness of breath. i'd like to get a better understanding of the cause of your shortness of breath before pursuing further treatment for your hypertension. i'd like you to discontinue the use of norvasc. we will have you follow up in about three weeks to just discuss your diabetes and further treatment recommendations. does that sound okay with you?
[patient] yeah, that sounds good. }}<|eot_id|>
