[patient] i drink moderately.
[doctor] okay. okay. all right. well, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. hey, dragon, show me the vital signs. okay. so, your vital signs look good. your heart sounds good. you do have a little bit of wheezing in your lungs, but that's not too bad. and your abdomen is a little bit tender, but it's not too bad. it's just a little bit tender in the top part of your belly. and i do hear a murmur in your heart, but that's nothing new. you've had that for a while. so, let's talk a little bit about a plan. um, i think that you might have something called gastritis, which is basically inflammation of your stomach. and i think this is because of too much caffeine and maybe a little bit of alcohol. so, i'm gon na recommend that you reduce your caffeine intake and reduce your alcohol intake. and i'm also going to prescribe you some zantac to help with the pain. and we'll get some blood work done. i'm gon na order a urinalysis, a pregnancy test, a cbc, and a comprehensive metabolic panel. and then we'll go from there. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and then for your diabetes, you're doing well. i just want to make a slight adjustment in your metformin. so, i'm gon na increase it to 1000 milligrams in the morning and 500 milligrams at night. and continue to monitor your blood sugars at home.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and then for your asthma, you're doing well. continue to take your flovent daily, even if you're not having any symptoms. it's gon na help prevent you from having symptoms in the future. and continue to use your albuterol as needed.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, i want to see you in four weeks to follow up. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. hey, dragon, finalize the note. }}<|eot_id|>
