dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, dr. smith. how are you?
[patient] hey, good. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well, thank you. so, i know that you're here because you're having some right elbow pain. can you tell me a little bit about what happened?
[patient] so, i was playing lacrosse and my son decided to take a swing at me with the stick and i think i'm going to be okay, but it's been a little sore.
[doctor] oh, that's not very nice. i'm sorry to hear that. are you able to move your elbow at all?
[patient] yeah, i can move it, but it's a little swollen and it hurts to bend it.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain when you move it?
[patient] it's a little bit, but not a lot.
[doctor] okay. and any pain when you straighten it?
[patient] just a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and any other symptoms? any fever or chills?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you taken any medicine for it?
[patient] no, i just iced it.
[doctor] okay. and how about any bruising?
[patient] yeah, there's a little bit of bruising.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let me take a listen to your heart. listen to your lungs. your lungs sound good. your heart is a three out of six, you have a systolic ejection murmur.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] your blood pressure is a little high, it's one fifty over ninety. you have a history of hypertension. are you taking your medication?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. and any problems with that?
[patient] no, i've been doing okay.
[doctor] okay. and how about your diabetes? how are you doing with that?
[patient] yeah, i've been doing good. i've been watching my diet.
[doctor] okay. i'm gon na go ahead and examine your elbow. okay, so when i press here, does that hurt?
[patient] yeah, that hurts a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and when i bend it like this?
[patient] yeah, a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and when i straighten it?
[patient] just a little bit.
[doctor] okay. so, there's some swelling and bruising here. otherwise, your range of motion is good. your x-ray was normal, so no fracture or bony abnormalities. i'm just gon na go ahead and order an x-ray. i'm just gon na go ahead and order an x-ray, just to make sure. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe you some ibuprofen eight hundred milligrams, take it twice a day. i'd like you to ice it in twenty-minute intervals three times a day. that should help with the pain and the swelling. and i'm gon na tell you to avoid playing lacrosse for a couple of weeks, just until it heals, and then you should be fine to continue playing normally.
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and i know you're on lisinopril for your hypertension. i want you to keep taking that. and for your diabetes, i'm gon na order a hemoglobin a1c. we'll just check that to make sure that you're not too high. and continue with the metformin five hundred milligrams daily.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] okay, do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay, great. do you need a refill on your lisinopril?
[patient] yeah, i do.
[doctor] okay. i'll go ahead and send that in to your pharmacy. okay, take care.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
