dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, mr. john. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well, thank you. so, i know that you had a bit of a heart failure exacerbation. how are you feeling?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm still a little short of breath.
[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and i'll take a look at your vitals here. so your blood pressure today is 128 over 72. your heart rate is 79, and your respiratory rate is 26. and your oxygen saturation is 99 % on room air.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all of those look good. let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm just gon na listen to your lungs. your lungs are clear. let me listen to your heart. your heart rate is regular. i do hear a two out of six systolic ejection murmur, but that's stable, which is good. and on your neck, i don't see any jugular venous distension, which is good. let's take a look at your lower extremities. there is trace edema to both of your lower extremities.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, i reviewed your echocardiogram. it shows that your ejection fraction is 55 %, which is good, but you do have abnormal diastolic filling and some mild to moderate mitral regurgitation.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, for your congestive heart failure, i know that this was an acute exacerbation, and i think that it was due to some dietary indiscretion and uncontrolled hypertension. so, i'm gon na continue you on the bumex, two milligrams once daily, and i'm gon na refer you to a nutritionist for some dietary education. i want you to continue to monitor your diet and avoid salty foods. i want you to weigh yourself every day, and if you gain three pounds in two days, i want you to give me a call.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? and for your hypertension, it was uncontrolled prior to your hospital visit. i know that you're currently on the cozaar, one hundred milligrams daily, and the norvasc, five milligrams once daily. i'm gon na continue you on those, but i do want to order a renal artery ultrasound, just to check on the blood vessels in your kidneys.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and then for your kidney disease, i know that you have stage three kidney disease, so i'm gon na go ahead and order some lab work, just to keep an eye on your kidney function.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? do you have any other questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll see you in three months, and you can call me if you have any questions or if you gain that weight.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
