[patient] yeah, so i was at a birthday party, and i was running up the stairs, and i ran into the railing and twisted my back. and i just twisted it really bad, and it's been bothering me ever since.
[doctor] okay. does it hurt anywhere else, like down your leg or anything like that?
[patient] no, it's just in the back.
[doctor] okay. and does anything make it worse or better?
[patient] it's worse when i lie flat. i can't really lie flat. and if i twist it, it hurts.
[doctor] okay. and have you taken anything for the pain?
[patient] i've taken some ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any back problems in the past?
[patient] no, this is the first time.
[doctor] okay. all right. and any surgeries in the past?
[patient] well, i did have a lumbar fusion.
[doctor] okay. all right. and have you been doing any exercises or anything to help with the pain?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let's take a look at you. i'm gon na do a quick physical exam. so i'm gon na press on your back here. does that hurt?
[patient] yeah, that hurts.
[doctor] okay. and does this hurt?
[patient] no, that's okay.
[doctor] all right. and i'm gon na do a straight leg raise. does that hurt?
[patient] no, that's okay.
[doctor] all right. and does this hurt?
[patient] yeah, that hurts.
[doctor] okay. and your sensation is okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] all right. well, let's take a look at your x-ray. so i reviewed your x-ray, and it looks like there's no signs of any acute fracture. it looks like you have a prior lumbar fusion with the hardware in good position. so what i'm gon na do is i'm gon na recommend you take some ice and heat. you can alternate them. and i want you to take motrin 800 mg three times a day with food. and if you're still having some pain, we can always follow up with you.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] all right. well, i'll see you next time you come in.
[patient] okay, thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
