dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey jordan how are you
[patient] i'm doing alright how about you
[doctor] good to see you so i see that you were in the emergency room a month ago for some palpitations and high blood pressure what's going on with that
[patient] yeah i was in the emergency room they said i had a panic attack but i was also drinking a lot of coffee that morning on an empty stomach and i was really nervous so i think that that might have contributed to it
[doctor] okay and since then have you had any other episodes
[patient] no i haven't had any other episodes since then
[doctor] okay and so i know that you've been monitoring your blood pressure at home how high is it running
[patient] it's running between 146 to 155
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any other symptoms when it's running that high
[patient] no i don't really feel anything i just know it's high
[doctor] okay and so i know that you've been trying to cut back on salt and i know that you have a family history of hypertension are you still watching that
[patient] yeah i'm watching my salt intake and i think i'm doing pretty well at cutting it down
[doctor] okay good and how about your exercise how's that going
[patient] i try to walk on my treadmill as often as i can
[doctor] okay alright so i know that your new primary care physician started you on a new medication called benicar hct how's that going
[patient] yeah i've been taking that for about a month now
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any side effects
[patient] no i haven't had any side effects
[doctor] okay good so looking at your past medical history i know that you've had hypertension for a long time is that correct
[patient] yes
[doctor] okay and do you have any other medical problems
[patient] nope i'm good
[doctor] okay and i know that your family history is significant for hypertension is that correct
[patient] yes it's a lot of people in my family
[doctor] okay so let's go ahead and take a look at your physical exam so on physical exam you have a normal rate and regular rhythm of heart sounds and normal pulses and breath sounds are normal and there's no tenderness on your abdomen and there's no edema on your extremities so looking at your thyroid profile from march first of this year everything looks good so let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan so it looks like you have resistant hypertension with your blood pressure running between 146 to 155 and you're currently on the maximal doses of three medications so i'm gon na add spironolactone to your regimen which will require monitoring of your potassium and sodium and we'll schedule you for a follow-up in two weeks to complete a basic metabolic panel and check your blood pressure and if we're not able to improve your blood pressure with spironolactone the next step would be sending you to the resistant hypertension clinic so i do want you to watch for some side effects of spironolactone such as gynecomastia and electrolyte disturbances and also an increased risk of dehydration so one sign to watch for would be dizziness so i'm gon na give you some materials on the american heart association website and you can access it for tips on lowering your salt intake and increasing your potassium intake your maximum salt intake should be one five hundred to two thousand milligrams per day and you should follow the dash diet and i encourage you to meet at least thirty minutes of walking most days
[patient] okay
[doctor] so i know that you're really active and i'm gon na encourage you to continue that so do you have any questions for me
[patient] no i don't think so
[doctor] okay alright well i'll see you in two weeks
[patient] okay
[doctor] alright thanks for coming in
[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>
