dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, teresa. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, but i'm having some trouble with my elbow.
[doctor] okay. what's going on with your elbow?
[patient] so i've been having some pain in my right elbow for the last four days. it's been really bothering me.
[doctor] okay. do you remember how this started?
[patient] well, i've been using a pottery wheel a lot more lately to make a bowl for my son's birthday. i think i overdid it.
[doctor] okay. have you injured it before?
[patient] no, never. this is the first time i've had any elbow pain.
[doctor] okay. does it hurt anywhere else?
[patient] no, just in the elbow. but it does go down into my arm a little bit.
[doctor] okay. does anything make it feel better or worse?
[patient] nothing really. i've tried ibuprofen and ice, but nothing seems to help.
[doctor] okay. how would you rate the pain on a scale from one to ten?
[patient] it's about a seven out of ten at its worst.
[doctor] okay. does it wake you up at night?
[patient] yes, if i roll over.
[doctor] okay. and what about your blood pressure? are you still checking it?
[patient] yes, i am. it's been in the 110s to 130s.
[doctor] okay. are you taking your lisinopril?
[patient] yes, i am. i take it every day.
[doctor] okay. and how about your diabetes? how are you doing with that?
[patient] it's okay. sometimes i forget to take my metformin.
[doctor] okay. and what have your blood sugars been running?
[patient] they've been running between 150 and 170.
[doctor] okay. and how often are you walking?
[patient] i walk in the morning and evening. about one to two miles a day.
[doctor] okay. do you have any other hobbies?
[patient] yes, i love working with ceramics and baking.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of things do you bake?
[patient] mostly cakes and cinnamon rolls for family gatherings.
[doctor] okay. let's do a quick review of systems. any other symptoms or problems?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. let me just check your vital signs. your blood pressure is 120 over 70. your pulse is 72. your respiratory rate is 18 breaths per minute. your oxygen saturation is 100 percent on room air. and your temperature is 97.9 degrees. let's check your weight. it looks like you've gained about five pounds since your last visit. so, let's talk a little bit about your elbow. i'm going to move your arm around a little bit. let me know if it hurts. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you do have some tenderness here on the inside of your elbow. and when you resist pronate your forearm, it hurts. and when you bend your wrist, it hurts a little bit. but i don't see any bruising or swelling. let's look at your x-ray. it doesn't show any fractures or anything else abnormal. so, it looks like you might have what we call medial epicondylitis. that's essentially inflammation of the tendons on the inside of your elbow. let's talk a little bit about how we can treat this. i'm going to recommend that you wear a sling on your right arm while you're awake to give it a little bit more support. i want you to ice it for twenty minutes three times a day. and i want you to take ibuprofen, six hundred milligrams every six hours with food for one week. i would also recommend that you hold off on making pottery for the next two weeks to let your elbow heal.
[patient] okay. that sounds good.
[doctor] and if you continue to have pain, we might need to consider formal physical therapy. and then for your diabetes, i'd like you to check your blood sugars every day. i'm going to increase your metformin to one thousand milligrams twice a day. it's very important that you take your medication on a regular basis, twice a day. i'd also like to refer you to diabetic counseling. they can give you some more information on what you can do to manage your diabetes. and for your hypertension, just continue taking your lisinopril ten milligrams a day. and continue with your walking routine. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. great. so, i'm going to order a hemoglobin a1c. we'll have you come back in two weeks to review the results of that and to see how you're doing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, thank you.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
