dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, sophia, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. so, i see here in my notes that you're here for some bilateral knee pain. how did this all start?
[patient] it started about six months ago.
[doctor] okay, and do you remember any specific injury or anything that happened that led to the pain?
[patient] no, i don't remember any injury. it just started.
[doctor] okay. and where exactly in your knees do you feel the pain?
[patient] it's deep, achy pain, and i feel it on the back of my knees.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any swelling or redness in your knees?
[patient] no, i don't see any swelling or redness.
[doctor] okay. and how does the pain affect you?
[patient] it's really painful when i'm getting up from sitting. it's also painful going up and down the stairs.
[doctor] okay. does it get any better?
[patient] yes, it gets better when i rest.
[doctor] okay. have you been doing anything to help the pain?
[patient] i've been icing them and wrapping them with an ace bandage.
[doctor] okay. and have you taken any medications for the pain?
[patient] i take ibuprofen or aleve every now and then.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other symptoms? like creaking or grinding?
[patient] yes, i do hear creaking.
[doctor] okay. have you ever injured your knees before?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. and what do you do for work?
[patient] i work from home.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of activities do you like to do?
[patient] i like to run.
[doctor] okay. how far do you usually run?
[patient] i used to run about five to six miles a day, but i can only go about. five hundred feet now.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other injuries in the past?
[patient] i broke my arm when i was in sixth grade.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms like numbness or tingling in your legs?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. well, let's take a look at your knees. i'm just gon na do a quick physical exam here. so, your vital signs look good. your heart sounds nice and regular. your lungs sound clear. and you don't have any swelling or redness in your legs. let's look at your knees here. i'm gon na check your patella. so, does this hurt?
[patient] yeah, it does.
[doctor] okay. let's move on to the other one. does this hurt?
[patient] yes, that one hurts too.
[doctor] okay. let's look at your strength here. so, your abduction strength is a little weak. it's about a three out of five. your other strength is normal. let's look at your lower extremities. so, i'm just gon na do a quick neurovascular exam here. your reflexes are normal. let's look at your knees again. so, i'm gon na press right here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and let me push right here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. so, you do have some tenderness to palpation of the retinaculum. let's do a quick patellar grind test. so, i'm gon na push down on your patella. does that hurt?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. let's squat down here. so, i'm gon na push down on your knee. does that hurt?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. so, you do have some pain with squatting. let's do a lachman test here. so, i'm gon na push on your knee. does that hurt?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. let's do a drawer test here. so, i'm gon na pull your knee. does that hurt?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. let's look at your x-rays. so, i reviewed the x-rays of your knees, and there's no evidence of any fractures or osteoarthritis. so, based on what you're experiencing and the exam, it sounds like you have patellofemoral pain syndrome. it's a pretty common condition. i'm gon na recommend that we start with some conservative treatment. i want you to start with some formal physical therapy to increase your lower extremity strength, mobility, and correct any incorrect running mechanics. i want you to take it easy on the running for now. you can continue taking ibuprofen or anti-inflammatories as needed for pain. and i want you to follow up with me soon. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, great. all questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay, well, i'll see you soon then. }}<|eot_id|>
