dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi kyle, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, but i've been having some back pain.
[doctor] okay, so i see here that you're here for low back pain. how long has that been going on?
[patient] it's been about two weeks now.
[doctor] okay. so what happened?
[patient] i was lifting a box of books and i felt a pop.
[doctor] okay. and have you been able to sit since then?
[patient] i've been sitting a lot, but it doesn't bother me.
[doctor] okay. and how about your job? how's that going?
[patient] i have a sedentary job, so i'm sitting most of the day.
[doctor] okay. and have you been able to continue your usual activities?
[patient] i try to exercise a few times a week, but i'm not as active as i used to be.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms like numbness or tingling in your legs or feet?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. how about any weakness or loss of control of your bladder or bowels?
[patient] no, none of that either.
[doctor] okay. have you taken any medication for the pain?
[patient] i've been taking ibuprofen and tylenol.
[doctor] okay. does that help?
[patient] it helps a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any surgeries in the past?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let's do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na check your vitals first. your blood pressure is one thirty over seventy, and your heart sounds nice and normal, and your lungs are clear. let me take a listen to your back. i don't appreciate any trauma or deformity. there's midline tenderness at the l four to five disc space. and there's some right-sided lumbar paravertebral tenderness. and i do appreciate pain with lumbar flexion, and there is a positive straight leg raise on the right side. let me check your neurovascular exam. sensation is normal. your patellar and achilles reflexes are symmetrical. i reviewed the results of your mri today, and it showed disc desiccation and a disc bulge with a paracentral disc herniation resulting in moderate right neural foraminal stenosis. so this means that you have a herniated disc in your lower back, and it's causing some irritation to the nerves, which is why you're having pain and some numbness and tingling in your leg. so i think we're gon na have to start with some conservative treatment. i'm gon na recommend that we do a cortisone injection into your back to help reduce the swelling and irritation around the disc. it's a pretty quick procedure. it's done in the office. i'll put you to sleep with some iv medication, and then i'll inject the medication into your back. and it should help with the pain and the numbness and tingling. do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and are you allergic to any medications?
[patient] no, i'm not allergic to any medications.
[doctor] okay. well, before we do the procedure, i just want to go over the risks. there's a risk of bleeding, infection, nerve damage, blood vessel damage, reaction to the medication, including skin changes, swelling, and also the risk of elevated glucose levels if you were diabetic.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so are you ready to proceed with the procedure?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. i'll call the nurse in to get you ready. thanks for coming in today.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
