dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi angela good to see you today so i know the nurse told you about dax and i'd like to tell dax a little bit about you so angela is an 81 year old female who's here for the evaluation of left knee pain so angela how are you doing today
[patient] i'm doing okay
[doctor] okay so i know the nurse told you a little bit about dax so dax is a smart artificial intelligence that's here to help me generate synthetic doctor-patient dialogues based on medical notes so i'm gon na be typing out notes as we go along and dax will be generating dialogues based on those notes so i'd like to start by asking you a few questions so i know you're here for left knee pain can you tell me a little bit about what happened
[patient] sure
[doctor] okay so i know the nurse said you fell and hurt your knee when was this
[patient] about a week ago
[doctor] okay and what were you doing when this happened
[patient] i was running around with my niece
[doctor] okay and did you hear a pop at the time of the injury
[patient] yes i did
[doctor] okay and did you feel like you twisted your knee or did you land funny
[patient] i think i twisted it
[doctor] okay and have you been able to walk on it since then
[patient] no i've been limping
[doctor] okay and where is the pain located in your knee
[patient] it's on the inside and outside
[doctor] okay so the medial and lateral aspects of your knee okay and on a scale of zero to ten how would you rate your pain
[patient] about a four
[doctor] okay and has it gotten worse or better since the initial injury
[patient] it's gotten worse
[doctor] okay and have you taken anything for the pain
[patient] i've taken tylenol
[doctor] okay and has that helped
[patient] it's helped a little bit but not much
[doctor] okay and have you been able to wrap it or do anything to help with the pain
[patient] i've wrapped it with kinesiology tape
[doctor] okay and do you have any medical problems that i should be aware of
[patient] i have an ulcer
[doctor] okay so you can't take ibuprofen so you've been taking tylenol and wrapping it with kinesiology tape have you had any other knee problems in the past
[patient] no not really
[doctor] okay alright so let's take a look at your knee so i'm gon na do a physical exam of your left knee and i'm gon na move your knee through some range of motion and let me know if you feel any pain okay
[patient] sure
[doctor] okay so i see that there is some edema and effusion in your knee and you do have some pain with flexion and extension of your knee as well as with extension there is a little bit of a click but it's not a significant one but i'm gon na do a few more maneuvers here so i'm gon na do a straight leg raise and i'm gon na pull your leg straight up and let me know if you feel any pain
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na do a lachman's test and i'm gon na pull your leg in and out and let me know if you feel any pain
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na do a varus and valgus stress test and i'm gon na push on the outside of your knee and then on the inside of your knee and let me know if you feel any pain
[patient] no
[doctor] okay so looking at your x-rays of your left knee i don't see any evidence of any fractures or dislocations and i don't see any other abnormalities so i'm gon na go over my assessment and plan with you so angela it looks like you have a possible mcl strain so for the first thing i'm gon na recommend is placing you in a knee immobilizer to provide some increased support for the next week i'm also gon na prescribe you some tramadol 50 milligrams to help with the pain and you can take tylenol as needed for any breakthrough pain i also want you to ice your knee three to four times a day for twenty to thirty minutes at a time and i want you to refrain from running for the next three weeks if your pain does not improve with the immobilizer i'm gon na recommend getting an mri if it's not better i wan na see you again in about a week to see how you're doing and if you have any questions feel free to ask
[patient] okay that sounds good
[doctor] alright thanks for coming in today }}<|eot_id|>
