dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, susan. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm a little stressed out from work, but i'm doing alright.
[doctor] okay. so you're here for a high blood pressure check. you know, your blood pressure has been running a little high. i know you've been on norvasc 10 milligrams daily, so we're gonna go ahead and we're gonna do some tests and we're gonna check your blood pressure and we're gonna see if we need to do anything with that. so, i know you've had high blood pressure for a while, but it seems like it's out of control lately. is that right?
[patient] yeah, it does seem like it's out of control lately. i've been checking it at home and it's been over 150.
[doctor] okay. and you've been taking the norvasc 10 milligrams daily. have you noticed any side effects from the norvasc?
[patient] no, i haven't noticed any side effects.
[doctor] okay. and you've had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no chest pain or shortness of breath.
[doctor] okay. and you've had a kidney transplant a few years ago. how's everything going with that?
[patient] everything is going well. i'm taking all of my immunosuppression medication.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any headaches?
[patient] yeah, i have had some headaches, but i'm not sure if it's from stress at work or my high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay. so let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so your vital signs look good. your blood pressure is a little high, but that's not surprising. your heart rate is good. your heart exam, i do appreciate a two over six systolic ejection murmur. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. your belly isn't tender. your extremities are nice and warm. there's no edema. and you do have a scar on your left flank from your kidney transplant, but that's healed. so, looking at your results, your creatinine is normal. your ekg is normal. so, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, for your first problem, your hypertension, i'd like to start you on carvedilol 25 milligrams twice a day. this is a blood pressure medication that can help bring your blood pressure down. i'd like to get a lipid panel and a metabolic panel. and i'd like to see you back in about two weeks to check your blood pressure and see how you're doing. for your second problem, your status post kidney transplant, everything looks good. you're doing well. your kidney function is stable. we'll continue you on your current medications. and i'll see you back in two weeks. any questions for me?
[patient] no questions.
[doctor] okay. great. i'll go ahead and get those tests ordered and we'll get you set up with the carvedilol. i'll see you in two weeks. okay?
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
