dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, hannah. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm just here for my blood sugar.
[doctor] so, i see that you're here for your blood sugar. so, can you tell me a little bit about what's going on with your blood sugar?
[patient] yeah, so i was just feeling really lightheaded and i was seeing spots in my vision and i was really dizzy and i went to the er and they said i had high blood sugar.
[doctor] okay. so, what did they do for you in the er?
[patient] they just gave me some iv fluids and told me to get into a routine and watch my diet.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms, like fever or chills or anything like that?
[patient] no, nothing out of the ordinary.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and any abdominal pain or burning when you urinate?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any joint pain or muscle aches?
[patient] no, my joints have been acting up a little bit, but nothing out of the ordinary for me.
[doctor] okay. and i see that you have a history of atrial fibrillation. how are you doing with that?
[patient] yeah, i've been doing alright. i feel like my heart racing when i'm anxious, but other than that, i haven't had any issues.
[doctor] okay. and are you still taking your metoprolol?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and how many milligrams are you taking?
[patient] 25 milligrams, twice a day.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking it twice a day?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any issues with that?
[patient] no, i've been doing alright.
[doctor] okay. and how about your acid reflux? how are you doing with that?
[patient] yeah, i've been doing really well. i've been taking the medication and it's been very helpful.
[doctor] okay. and what medication are you taking for that?
[patient] protonix.
[doctor] okay. and how many milligrams are you taking?
[patient] 40 milligrams once a day.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking it once a day?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any issues with that?
[patient] no, i've been doing alright.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical conditions?
[patient] yeah, i have osteoarthritis.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with that?
[patient] it's been acting up a little bit, but nothing out of the ordinary for me.
[doctor] okay. so, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, on your physical exam, your thyroid is a little bit enlarged, but not tender. there are no carotid bruits. your lungs are clear. your heart is an irregular rate and rhythm. your abdomen is nice and soft, and there's no edema in your lower extremities.
[doctor] so, based on your blood glucose, it's elevated. your hemoglobin a1c is also elevated. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order a complete metabolic panel to further evaluate that. i'm gon na go ahead and initiate metformin 500 milligrams twice a day. i want you to make some dietary modifications. i'm gon na give you a glucometer to monitor your glucose levels at home. and i want you to follow up with me in two weeks to check your blood glucose levels.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? and for your atrial fibrillation, i want you to continue taking your metoprolol 25 milligrams twice a day. i'm gon na go ahead and refill that for you today.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? and for your acid reflux, i want you to continue taking your protonix 40 milligrams once a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll see you in two weeks then.
[patient] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
