dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi christine. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. so i know that i saw you in 2019 and you know, you were having some issues with your blood pressure and some depression. how are you doing with those?
[patient] i'm doing well with my depression. i'm taking my medication, i'm going to therapy once a week, and i'm sleeping well at night.
[doctor] okay, that's good. and how many hours of sleep are you getting?
[patient] i'm getting eight hours of sleep.
[doctor] okay, good. and do you have any thoughts of harming yourself or others?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. and have you checked your blood pressure at all?
[patient] yes, i have. it's been fluctuating a little bit lately.
[doctor] okay. and have you had a normal reading in the last couple of weeks?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking your medication as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and how's your diet been? have you been watching what you eat?
[patient] no, it's been a little all over the place.
[doctor] okay. and how's your right carpal tunnel release doing?
[patient] it's doing well. i don't have any numbness or tingling in my hands or fingers.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any headaches?
[patient] yes, i have. but i thought it was just from my increased screen time.
[doctor] okay. and are you working more hours?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. your vital signs are looking good. your blood pressure is a little elevated, but we can work on that. and your neck is supple, no thyroid gland is enlarged. your lungs are clear, and your heart is regular rate and rhythm. i don't hear any murmurs or extra heart sounds. your neurological exam is normal. your mood and affect are appropriate. your grip strength is equal. and you're neurologically intact.
[patient] great.
[doctor] so i'm gon na go ahead and review your results. and all of your lab results are looking good. so let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. for your depression, you're doing well. you're taking your medication, you're going to therapy, and you're sleeping well. so let's just continue with that. for your hypertension, your blood pressures have been fluctuating lately, and i think we need to increase your medication. i'm going to increase your lisinopril to 10 milligrams once a day. and i want you to continue to monitor your blood pressures at home and follow up with me in a month. and for your right carpal tunnel release, you're doing well, two years postoperatively, and you're asymptomatic. so let's just continue to monitor that. if you have any symptoms, give us a call. and do you have any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll see you in a month then.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] hey, dragon, finalize the note. }}<|eot_id|>
