dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, brittany. how are you?
[patient] hi, doctor. i'm good. how are you?
[doctor] good. so i know that you were here in august of 2019. so i know it's been a while. and i know that you were having some issues with your stomach and your bowels. so i know we had a lot of discussions about that. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm still having some issues.
[doctor] okay. so what's been going on? you know, i know that you were having some problems with your stomach and your bowels. what's been going on?
[patient] well, i've been having some cramping and sharp pains.
[doctor] okay. and when did this start?
[patient] it's been going on for a while.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing? have you been eating okay? are you eating okay?
[patient] i've been eating alright. i've been trying to watch what i eat. i had some shrimp the other day and it gave me some pain.
[doctor] okay. and how about any other foods? are there any other foods that give you pain?
[patient] well, i had some chicken alfredo and that made me have some diarrhea.
[doctor] okay. and do you think it's the alfredo or the chicken?
[patient] i don't think it's the alfredo.
[doctor] okay. and what about drinking? do you drink a lot of alcohol?
[patient] i drink a couple of drinks when i'm out. tequila or brown liquor. and sometimes i have a martini.
[doctor] okay. and how often do you drink?
[patient] like, maybe a couple of times a month.
[doctor] okay. and do you drink every day?
[patient] no, not every day. just when i'm out.
[doctor] okay. and what about soda? do you drink a lot of soda?
[patient] no, i've been trying to cut back on that.
[doctor] okay. and how's that going?
[patient] it's been okay. i've been doing alright.
[doctor] okay. and what about your bowel movements? how often do you go to the bathroom?
[patient] i go like, two to three times a day.
[doctor] okay. and are you passing stools or are you passing diarrhea?
[patient] i'm passing stools.
[doctor] okay. and how about nausea? are you having any nausea?
[patient] yeah, sometimes i get nauseous.
[doctor] okay. and how often?
[patient] not every day, but sometimes.
[doctor] okay. and what do you do for that?
[patient] i take some medication.
[doctor] okay. and what medication?
[patient] i take reglan.
[doctor] okay. and how often do you take that?
[patient] as needed.
[doctor] okay. and what about the last time you were here, we talked about some other medications. we talked about elavil and buspar. have you tried those?
[patient] no, i haven't tried those yet.
[doctor] okay. and what about bentyl? do you take that?
[patient] yeah, i take that.
[doctor] okay. and how often do you take that?
[patient] i take it as needed.
[doctor] okay. and what about your diet? have you been watching what you eat?
[patient] yeah, i've been trying to watch what i eat.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of foods have you been eating?
[patient] i've been eating a lot of greasy foods.
[doctor] okay. and do you think that's making your symptoms worse?
[patient] probably.
[doctor] okay. well, i think we need to talk about some dietary changes. i think we need to talk about some lifestyle changes. so i know that you were having some issues with your stress and your sleep. how's your stress level?
[patient] it's still pretty high.
[doctor] okay. and how about your sleep? how's your sleep?
[patient] it's still pretty bad.
[doctor] okay. well, i think we need to talk about some stress management and some sleep management. so i'm going to prescribe you some medication. i'm going to prescribe you elavil 25 milligrams at bedtime. and i want you to start taking that. i also want you to continue taking the bentyl. and i want you to take that 20 milligrams as needed 30 to 45 minutes before you eat at a restaurant. and if you're still having nausea, i want you to take some zofran. but i want you to stop taking the reglan. and i want you to try to avoid any heavy foods. i want you to try to avoid any greasy foods. and i want you to try to cut back on your alcohol consumption. i want you to try to cut back on your drinking. and i want you to try to get some better sleep. i want you to try to get some better stress management. so i'm going to give you some instructions. i want you to send me a message in one month. i want you to let me know how you're doing. and i want you to come back in one month. and if you're still having issues, we can adjust your medications. and we can talk about some other things that we can do to help you.
[patient] okay. sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. alright. well, it was good seeing you. i'm glad we could talk.
[patient] yeah, same here.
[doctor] okay. take care of yourself.
[patient] you too.
[doctor] alright. bye-bye.
[patient] bye-bye. }}<|eot_id|>
