dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, miss taylor, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, good to see you.
[doctor] good to see you too. so, i know we've talked a lot about your hypertension and your alcohol use disorder. let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam and then we'll talk about my assessment and plan.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] okay, so i reviewed your vitals here, and your blood pressure is 140 over 90. and your heart rate is 68. so, your heart rate is pretty good, but your blood pressure is a little higher than i'd like to see.
[patient] yeah, i've been having some problems with that.
[doctor] okay. so, i know we had discussed that you were having some issues with your blood pressure. and i know that you've been taking the lisinopril, 20 milligrams once a day. and the hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams once a day. have you had any side effects from those medications?
[patient] yeah, i did have some side effects. i felt really lethargic, and i had some headaches. and i felt like there was like, like, a swooshing in my left ear. i only took half of the pill, so i'm not sure if that was from that or if i just felt that way.
[doctor] okay. well, we can talk about that a little bit more. but, you know, i know that you've been taking those medications. and i know that you've been checking your blood pressure. and i know that your blood pressure has been running a little higher than we'd like to see. and i know that you've been having some issues with your alcohol use disorder. so, i'm just wondering, how are you doing with that? how are you doing with stopping drinking?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm still drinking a little bit. i'm trying to cut back, but it's hard. i don't want to stop drinking, but i know it's not good for me.
[doctor] okay. well, you know, i think that's a really good step, just acknowledging that you want to cut back. and i think that's a really good step, and i think that we can work with that. so, i'm gon na talk to you a little bit about my assessment and my plan. so, for your first problem, your alcohol use disorder, you know, i think that you're doing a good job just acknowledging that you want to cut back. and i think that's a really good step. and i think that we can work with that. so, i'm gon na start you on some naltrexone. and that's gon na help you with that. and i'm gon na start you on the injectable form. and we're gon na start that on may 17th. and we'll go from there. and i'll see you back in a couple of weeks to check on that. and then, for your second problem, your hypertension, you know, i think that we need to continue you on the lisinopril. and i think that we need to continue you on the hydrochlorothiazide. and i think that your blood pressure will probably improve significantly if you can cut back on drinking. and i think that's a really good thing for you to work on. so, let's continue you on the lisinopril, 10 milligrams once a day. and let's continue you on the hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams once a day. and i want to see you back in a couple of weeks to check on that. and i want to see you back here in about two weeks to check on your blood pressure. and we'll go from there. any questions?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, it was good to see you. i'll talk to you soon.
[patient] okay, thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
