dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] hi, i'm doing well, thanks.
[doctor] hey, hey, so i see here that you're having some right elbow pain, what's going on?
[patient] yeah, so i was playing lacrosse over the weekend and my son accidentally hit me with a stick, so i'm having some pain in my elbow.
[doctor] okay, so did you fall or was it just a direct hit?
[patient] it was a direct hit.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit more about the pain, is it a sharp pain or a dull pain?
[patient] it's more of a dull pain.
[doctor] okay, and is it constant or does it come and go?
[patient] it's pretty constant.
[doctor] okay, and have you been able to move your elbow at all?
[patient] yeah, i can move it, but it's a little swollen.
[doctor] okay, and is there any bruising?
[patient] yeah, there's some bruising.
[doctor] okay, and have you taken anything for the pain?
[patient] yeah, i took some ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay, and how much ibuprofen did you take?
[patient] i took 600 milligrams.
[doctor] okay, and how many times did you take it?
[patient] i took it twice.
[doctor] okay, and did you take it before or after the injury?
[patient] after the injury.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit about your medical history, do you have any medical conditions?
[patient] yeah, i have high blood pressure and diabetes.
[doctor] okay, and are you on any medications for those?
[patient] yeah, i'm on lisinopril for my blood pressure and metformin for my diabetes.
[doctor] okay, and have you had any previous injuries?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit about your family medical history?
[patient] yeah, my dad had a heart attack a few years ago.
[doctor] okay, and is he on any medications?
[patient] yeah, he's on atenolol and aspirin.
[doctor] okay, and does he have any other medical conditions?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit about your lifestyle?
[patient] yeah, i try to eat healthy and exercise a few times a week.
[doctor] okay, and do you smoke or drink?
[patient] i don't smoke, but i do drink.
[doctor] okay, and how often do you drink?
[patient] probably a few times a week.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit about your symptoms, any other symptoms you're having?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay, and can you tell me a little bit about your sleep?
[patient] yeah, i sleep pretty well.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any allergies?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and examine you, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to start with your vital signs, your blood pressure is a little elevated, it's 150 over 90.
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, and your heart rate is 70 and your oxygen saturation is 98 percent on room air.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and listen to your heart and lungs, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, so your heart sounds good, and your lungs are clear.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and examine your elbow, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to press on your elbow, and i'm going to move it around, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, and it's a little tender to the touch, and you have some swelling, and there's some bruising, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, and you have a grade two out of six systolic ejection murmur, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and get an x-ray of your elbow, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and look at the results of your x-ray, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, so it looks like you don't have any fractures, and it looks like you have a contusion, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so i'm going to go ahead and give you a prescription for some ibuprofen, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, and i want you to take 800 milligrams twice a day, and i also want you to ice your elbow for 20 minutes three times a day, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, and i also want you to avoid playing lacrosse for the next couple of weeks, just until your elbow heals, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, and i also want you to keep up with your dietary modifications for your diabetes, and i'm going to order a hemoglobin a1c to evaluate if we need to adjust your medications, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, and i'm also going to keep you on lisinopril 20 milligrams a day for your high blood pressure, and i want you to keep up with your dietary modifications, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, and i'm going to keep you on metformin 500 milligrams a day for your diabetes, and i want you to keep up with your dietary modifications, and i'm going to order a hemoglobin a1c to evaluate if we need to adjust your medications, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any other appointments that you need to schedule?
[patient] yeah, i have a follow-up appointment for my diabetes.
[doctor] okay, and when is that appointment?
[patient] it's in two weeks.
[doctor] okay, and i'll make sure to schedule that for you, okay?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay, well, it was nice seeing you, and i'll see you soon.
[patient] yeah, you too. }}<|eot_id|>
