dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright, i'm a little nervous, i guess.
[doctor] yeah, i know, i'm sure it's a little weird coming in here, but i'm here to help you, so don't you worry.
[patient] okay, thanks.
[doctor] so, you know, i know you've been told you've got a high cholesterol, and we need to talk about that.
[patient] yeah, i was told i've got a high cholesterol, and i need to do something about it.
[doctor] okay, well, let's start with that. so, can you tell me a little bit about your cholesterol levels? how did you find out you had high cholesterol?
[patient] yeah, i just went in for a routine check up, and they told me that my cholesterol was high.
[doctor] okay, and did they tell you what your numbers were?
[patient] yeah, they told me that my total cholesterol was 210.
[doctor] okay, and have you had any problems with your heart or anything like that?
[patient] no, i've been feeling fine, i just got a little worried because i heard that high cholesterol can be bad for you.
[doctor] yeah, it can be, but we'll get that taken care of. so, can you tell me a little bit about your diet? do you eat a lot of fatty foods?
[patient] i eat a lot of pizza and burgers, but i also like to eat salads and stuff like that too.
[doctor] okay, and do you exercise at all?
[patient] yeah, i like to ride my bike on the trails.
[doctor] that's great. so, do you smoke?
[patient] no, i don't smoke.
[doctor] okay, great. and do you have any family history of heart disease or high cholesterol?
[patient] yeah, my cousin died of a heart attack in his 40's.
[doctor] okay, that's good to know. and what about your parents? did they have high cholesterol or heart disease?
[patient] no, they're still alive and healthy.
[doctor] okay, great. well, let's take a look at your vitals. (pause) okay, your blood pressure looks good. i'm just going to listen to your heart and lungs. (pause) okay, everything sounds good there. now, i'm going to do a physical exam. (pause) okay, everything looks good. i don't see any xanthomas, which is good. now, let's talk about your test results. your recent cholesterol level was 210, and we're going to do some more tests to see what's going on. we'll do a full cholesterol panel, and we'll also check your hemoglobin a1c, cmp, thyroid study, and liver panel.
[patient] okay, what does that all mean?
[doctor] well, it means we're going to check a lot of things to see what's going on with your body. we'll check your cholesterol levels again, and we'll also check your blood sugar levels, and make sure your thyroid is working okay, and your liver is working okay.
[patient] okay, got it.
[doctor] yeah, and we'll also do some genetic testing to see if this is something that you were born with or if it's something that happened later in life.
[patient] okay, that sounds like a lot of tests.
[doctor] it is, but don't worry, we'll get it all taken care of. so, i'm going to recommend that you follow a balanced diet with a variety of foods that are low in saturated fat and sugars, and we'll also recommend that you stay active. and we'll refer you to a nutritionist to help you with that.
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] yeah, and i'm also going to order some medications to help lower your cholesterol levels. we'll start with a statin, and we'll go from there.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] and i want you to follow up with me in about 3 to 6 months, after you've met with the nutritionist, and we'll check your cholesterol levels again, and see how you're doing.
[patient] okay, sounds like a plan.
[doctor] yeah, it is. and don't forget, it's also important to get regular exercise, and to watch what you eat. and if you have any questions or concerns, just give me a call.
[patient] okay, will do.
[doctor] great. well, that's all for today. i'll have my nurse come in and give you the orders, and we'll get you scheduled for your follow up appointment.
[patient] okay, thanks, doc.
[doctor] you're welcome. take care, and don't forget to call if you have any questions.
[patient] will do, thanks again.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
