dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm having some chest pain.
[doctor] chest pain? okay, so when did this start?
[patient] it started a few days ago.
[doctor] okay. have you been exercising or doing anything strenuous?
[patient] i've been doing some light exercise, but i've been having this pain for a while now.
[doctor] okay. and when you exercise, does the pain get worse?
[patient] it does.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms like shortness of breath or dizziness?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. have you had any chest pain before?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any medical conditions?
[patient] i have diabetes.
[doctor] okay, and are you taking any medications for your diabetes?
[patient] yes, i'm taking metformin.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any family history of heart disease?
[patient] yes, my parents had heart disease.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any blood work done recently?
[patient] no, not recently.
[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm going to check your blood pressure. it's a little high, 140 over 90.
[patient] yeah, i've been having some swelling in my legs.
[doctor] okay. let me just check your heart. your heart sounds good. i don't hear any murmurs. and your lungs are clear. i don't hear any wheezes or rales.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and your abdomen is soft. i don't feel any tenderness. and your ankles have some swelling, but it's just a little bit.
[patient] yeah, that's where my swelling is.
[doctor] okay. and let me check your legs. you do have a little bit of edema in your ankles. it's just a little bit, but we can work on that.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so let's talk about your chest pain. i think it's probably related to your diabetes and your family history of heart disease. i'm going to order an ekg, and we're going to do some blood work. i'm going to order a hemoglobin a1c. it's been a while since you had one, so we'll check that out. and i'm also going to order a lipid panel, just to make sure everything is okay.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm going to start you on some medication. i'm going to start you on some baby aspirin, 81 milligrams a day. and i'm going to give you a prescription for some nitroglycerin. you can take it as needed for your chest pain. and i'm also going to give you a prescription for some sublingual nitroglycerin. if you have chest pain, you can take that. if it doesn't work after about five minutes, you should go to the emergency room.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i want you to follow up with me in two weeks. i'm also going to refer you to a cardiologist. i want you to get your blood pressures checked, and i want you to get an echocardiogram. i want to make sure everything is okay.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm going to start you on a medication to help with your blood pressure. i'm going to start you on hydrochlorothiazide. it's a low dose, and it should help with your swelling.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i want you to keep your appointment with ophthalmology. they're going to check your eyes. i want to make sure everything is okay.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i want you to keep your appointment with me in two weeks. i want to check on you. i want to make sure everything is okay.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm going to give you some instructions. i want you to monitor your blood pressures at home, and i want you to report them to me. i want to see how you're doing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and if you have any questions or concerns, just give me a call. i'm here to help you.
[patient] okay, thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
