dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi there, how are you today?
[patient] hi, i'm doing well, thanks.
[doctor] great, so you're here for your annual exam.
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] so tell me a little bit about what's been going on with you. how have you been doing?
[patient] i've been doing well, i just started working at a bakery this summer.
[doctor] wow, congratulations on the new job.
[patient] thanks.
[doctor] so how's that going? is it what you expected?
[patient] yeah, it's been good.
[doctor] great. and how's your diabetes been? have you had any issues with that?
[patient] yeah, my diabetes has been a little uncontrolled. my blood sugars have been fluctuating a lot.
[doctor] okay, that's not good. can you tell me a little bit more about that? what's been causing that?
[patient] i think it's just because of my diet. i've been eating a lot of sweets.
[doctor] okay. have you been taking your medication as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and have you missed any doses?
[patient] no, i haven't missed any doses.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood pressure? has that been okay?
[patient] yeah, my blood pressure has been good.
[doctor] okay, that's good. and have you been sleeping okay?
[patient] yeah, i've been sleeping well. i've been able to get a full 8 hours.
[doctor] great. and have you had any thoughts of self-harm or suicidal ideations?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay, that's good. so i'm just going to go ahead and do a quick physical exam. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so your heart sounds good. your lungs are clear. your neck is supple. i don't feel any lymph nodes. i do appreciate a 2 out of 6 systolic ejection fraction murmur.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and your grip strength is equal bilaterally. your neurologically intact.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so let me just go ahead and look at your labs real quick. your hemoglobin a1c is elevated.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so i'm gon na go ahead and order some labs for you. i'm gon na continue you on your metformin twice a day. i want you to check your fasting blood glucose levels each morning and call them in about 2 weeks. we'll follow up in about 2 months and we'll discuss further treatment recommendations.
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] and how about your blood pressure? how's that been?
[patient] it's been good.
[doctor] okay, so i'm gon na continue you on your lisinopril 10 milligrams once a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i want you to come back and see me in about 2 months. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay, great. well, i'll see you in 2 months.
[patient] okay, thanks.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
