dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm good, thanks. i've been feeling pretty tired and just feeling a little bit under the weather.
[doctor] okay. so you're feeling a little bit tired and under the weather. have you been doing anything new or stressful that might be causing that?
[patient] no, not really. i think it's just been a lot of work and just feeling a little bit run down.
[doctor] okay. well, we can definitely work on getting you feeling better. so you said you've been feeling tired. have you noticed any other symptoms like fever or chills?
[patient] no, not really. just feeling tired and a little bit nauseous.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any rashes or anything like that on your skin?
[patient] actually, i did get an insect bite on my last visit. i was out hiking and got bit by something.
[doctor] okay. and did you get that checked out?
[patient] yeah, i did. they did a lyme titer and it came back positive.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about your medical history. you have type two diabetes, is that correct?
[patient] yes, that's correct.
[doctor] okay. and have you been taking your metformin?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and have you been monitoring your blood sugars at all?
[patient] yeah, i have. they've been okay, but sometimes they're a little high or low, but nothing too crazy.
[doctor] okay. and what about your blood pressure? you have hypertension. have you been monitoring that?
[patient] yeah, i have. it's been good. i've been avoiding salty foods and taking my lisinopril.
[doctor] okay. great. that's good to hear. so, i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam on you. i'm gon na start with your abdomen. how are you feeling in your stomach?
[patient] i'm not really feeling anything.
[doctor] okay. and are you having any pain or diarrhea?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and how about your joints? are you having any joint pain?
[patient] yeah, i have been having a lot of pain in my elbows and my body aches.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any rashes on your skin?
[patient] yeah, i do have a rash on my stomach.
[doctor] okay. let me just take a look. (pause) okay, i do see a small bullseye rash on your left abdominal quadrant. i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick exam of your joints. (pause) okay, i do appreciate some swelling and pain to palpation of your elbow joints bilaterally.
[patient] yeah, that's what's been bothering me.
[doctor] okay. and have you been able to eat?
[patient] no, not really. i've just been eating crackers and stuff.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about your labs. we did a lyme titer and it came back positive. i'm gon na go ahead and order some other labs to make sure we're not missing anything else. (pause) i'm also gon na go ahead and prescribe you some doxycycline for 3 weeks. we'll touch base with an infectious disease doctor to make sure we don't need to do anything else. i want to see you back in a week for a follow-up. okay?
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na go ahead and continue you on your lisinopril. i'm also gon na order a lipid panel. and for your diabetes, i'm gon na go ahead and order a hemoglobin a1c. and i want to see you back in a week. okay?
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. any questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right, i'll see you in a week.
[patient] thanks.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
