dialogue is: {{ [doctor] okay, so, uh, can you tell me a little bit about what brings you in today?
[patient] yeah, i've been having some issues with my blood sugar, and i've been eating a lot of sweets over the holidays.
[doctor] okay, okay. so you've been having some high blood sugar. have you noticed any other symptoms like dizziness or lightheadedness?
[patient] yeah, i've been feeling really lightheaded, and i've been seeing spots in my vision. i went to the er and they told me that my blood sugar was high, and they gave me iv fluids.
[doctor] okay, okay. and did they give you any medication for that?
[patient] no, they just told me to watch my diet and get back into a routine.
[doctor] okay, okay. so have you noticed any other symptoms like chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, nothing like that. just the dizziness and lightheadedness.
[doctor] okay, okay. and do you have any other medical conditions like high blood pressure or diabetes?
[patient] yeah, i have atrial fibrillation, and i've been taking metoprolol for that.
[doctor] okay, okay. and have you noticed any issues with that?
[patient] no, not really. just when i'm feeling anxious, my heart starts racing.
[doctor] okay, okay. and what about your acid reflux? have you been having any issues with that?
[patient] no, i've been doing well with that. i've been taking protonix and it's been really helpful.
[doctor] okay, okay. so let's take a look at your vitals. your blood pressure is a little high, but that's not uncommon for you. your heart rate is irregular, but that's probably due to your atrial fibrillation. your lungs are clear, and your abdomen is soft. i do want to check your thyroid, and it does seem a little enlarged, but it's not tender.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so let's talk a little bit about your diabetes. your blood sugar was elevated in the er, and i want to get a complete metabolic panel to see what's going on. i'm also going to prescribe you metformin 500 mg twice daily. i want you to start making some dietary modifications and we'll get you a glucometer so you can monitor your blood sugar at home.
[patient] okay, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, and i know you're staying with family during the holidays, but i want you to try to get back into your routine as soon as you can. and for your atrial fibrillation, we'll continue you on metoprolol 25 mg twice daily. i'll also refill that for you today. and for your acid reflux, you can continue the protonix 40 mg daily.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay, great. i'll have my nurse come in and get you set up with the metformin and the glucometer. and we'll get you checked out and you can go home.
[patient] okay, sounds good. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
