dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. ross. how are you?
[patient] hi. i'm good. thanks.
[doctor] good to meet you. so, you know, i'm a nurse practitioner, and i'm here to help you with your healthcare needs today. can you tell me a little bit about what brings you in?
[patient] yeah, i just wanted to get a full-spectrum std test done. i recently found out that my partner of three years has been having multiple partners, and i want to make sure i'm okay.
[doctor] okay. so you've been having some symptoms. can you tell me more about those symptoms?
[patient] yeah, i've just been noticing a change in my discharge, and it smells bad, and it's just been really uncomfortable. the right side of my vagina is getting really sore.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any fever or chills?
[patient] no, no fever or chills.
[doctor] okay. and how long has this been going on?
[patient] it started about a week ago.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any abnormal pap smears in the past?
[patient] actually, i had an abnormal pap smear when i was about 20, but all the others since then have been normal.
[doctor] okay. and how long ago was your last pap smear?
[patient] about six months ago.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions about stds or anything like that?
[patient] no, i just want to make sure i'm okay.
[doctor] okay. all right, so let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so i'm just going to do a quick exam. i'm gon na look at your external genitalia. everything looks normal. your labia majora and labia minora look normal. your physiological discharge is normal. the color and odor are normal. i'm just gon na do a quick cervical exam. your cervix is normal. your vaginal wall is normal. i'm not feeling any cervical motion tenderness or any masses. and i'm gon na go ahead and get some swabs for std testing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so we'll just take those swabs and get them sent off to the lab. we'll call you with the results. and i'll also order some std tests, including gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. you are at high risk due to your abnormal pap smear in the past and your partner having multiple partners.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. all right, so i'm gon na go ahead and order all those tests. we'll call you with the results. and we'll also get you set up with some treatment if you need it. does that sound okay?
[patient] yeah, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. great. all right, well, thank you so much for coming in today. i'll talk to you soon.
[patient] thanks. }}<|eot_id|>
