dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, teresa, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. i've been having some elbow pain.
[doctor] okay. so, you've been having elbow pain. can you tell me more about that?
[patient] yeah, it started about four days ago. i think it's from me using the pottery wheel. i've been trying to make a bowl for my son.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any injuries to your elbow before?
[patient] no, not that i'm aware of.
[doctor] okay. and how would you rate your pain level?
[patient] it's about a seven out of ten.
[doctor] okay. and does it wake you up at night?
[patient] yeah, if i roll over.
[doctor] okay. and have you tried ibuprofen or ice for the pain?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and are you able to work with the pottery wheel?
[patient] no, i'm not.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] i have high blood pressure and diabetes type two.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications for those?
[patient] yeah, i'm taking lisinopril for the blood pressure and metformin for the diabetes.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking those as prescribed?
[patient] sometimes i forget to take the metformin.
[doctor] okay. and how often are you walking?
[patient] i walk about a mile a day.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any changes in your blood sugars?
[patient] sometimes they're a little high.
[doctor] okay. and what do they get up to?
[patient] up to 170.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm going to go ahead and do a physical exam on you. i'm gon na listen to your heart and lungs and do a physical exam of your elbow.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, your blood pressure is one twenty over seventy. your heart and lungs sound good. and on your physical exam of your elbow, you do have some tenderness on the inside of your elbow. you have some pain with bending and flexing of your wrist. and i'm gon na order an x-ray of your elbow to make sure that we don't have any fractures.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, the x-ray of your elbow looks good. we don't see any fractures. but it does look like you have some inflammation and tendonitis in your elbow.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na recommend that we treat you conservatively. i want you to wear a sling on your right arm while you're awake. i want you to ice your elbow for twenty minutes, three times a day. i want you to take ibuprofen, six hundred milligrams, every six hours with food for a week. and i want you to hold off on creating pottery for the next two weeks.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'm also gon na increase your metformin to one thousand milligrams, twice a day. and i want you to check your blood sugars every day. i'm also gon na order a hemoglobin a1c to get a better look at your long-term blood sugar levels.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na refer you to diabetic counseling to help you with managing your diabetes.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to continue taking your lisinopril. and i want you to continue with your walking routine.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, we'll follow up with you in two weeks to check on your progress.
[patient] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
