dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, dennis, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm having some issues with my heel. i'm a triathlete and i've been doing a lot of training, but i've been having some pain in my heel and it's been really bothering me.
[doctor] okay, well, let's talk a little bit about your symptoms. so, you've been doing a lot of training and you've been having pain in your heel. can you tell me more about that? when did it start?
[patient] it started about 10 days ago. i was training for a triathlon and i've been doing a lot of running and biking and swimming. and i just started to feel this pain in my heel.
[doctor] okay, so it started about 10 days ago and you've been having pain in your heel. have you noticed any other symptoms?
[patient] yeah, the pain has been radiating up into my calf. it's been really sore. and it's been getting worse over time.
[doctor] okay, so you've been having pain in your heel and it's radiating up into your calf. have you noticed any other symptoms like swelling or redness?
[patient] no, not really. just the pain.
[doctor] okay. have you been doing anything to make the pain better?
[patient] no, i've just been trying to take it easy and rest. but it's still really sore.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to go ahead and do a physical exam. can you please remove your shoes and socks?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm going to press on your heel and calf. can you tell me where it hurts?
[patient] yeah, it hurts right here.
[doctor] okay. and can you please squeeze your calf?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and can you please point to where it hurts?
[patient] right here.
[doctor] okay. and can you please bend your foot down towards your shin?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and can you please point to where it hurts?
[patient] right here.
[doctor] okay. and can you please stand up and walk around the room for me?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to check your vitals and i'm going to order some x-rays of your ankle. have you had any problems with your ankles in the past?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and have you been taking any medications?
[patient] no, i haven't been taking anything.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to go ahead and prescribe you some ibuprofen to help with the pain. and i'm also going to give you a referral for physical therapy to help with your ankle.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm going to go ahead and prescribe you 3 tablets of ibuprofen every 6 hours for pain. and i'm going to give you a referral for physical therapy. and i want you to take at least 1 week off from your training to recover from this.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to follow up with me in 7 to 10 days to check on your progress. sound good?
[patient] yeah, that sounds good. thanks, doc.
[doctor] you're welcome. take care. }}<|eot_id|>
