dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay, i'm just trying to get over this heart problem that i had.
[doctor] okay, so i'm looking at your chart here and it says that you were in the hospital for an acute on chronic congestive heart failure. how are you feeling?
[patient] i'm feeling a little better, but i'm still having some problems with my ankles swelling.
[doctor] okay, and how much weight did you gain?
[patient] i gained about 5 pounds.
[doctor] okay, and how are you feeling otherwise? are you short of breath or any chest pain?
[patient] no, i'm not short of breath and i don't have any chest pain.
[doctor] okay, and have you noticed any sleep disturbances?
[patient] no, i'm sleeping fine.
[doctor] okay, and how about your diet? are you watching your salt intake?
[patient] i'm trying to, but it's hard.
[doctor] okay, well let's talk a little bit about your medical history. i see that you have a history of hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease. have you been taking your medications?
[patient] yes, i've been taking my medications, but i think i need to start watching my diet a little better.
[doctor] okay, well let's talk about your medications. you're taking bumex 2 milligrams once a day, cozaar 100 milligrams a day, and norvasc 5 milligrams once a day. are you taking those as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay, and have you noticed any side effects from those medications?
[patient] no, i haven't noticed any side effects.
[doctor] okay, and have you had any other medical problems in the past?
[patient] no, i've been healthy otherwise.
[doctor] okay, well let's do a quick physical exam. so your blood pressure is 128 over 72, your heart rate is 79, your respiratory rate is 26, and your oxygen saturation is 99 percent. i don't hear any abnormal heart sounds. your lungs are clear, and you have some edema in your ankles. i'm going to go ahead and order some lab work, including a complete blood count and a blood chemistry panel. i also want to order a renal artery ultrasound to evaluate your kidney function. i'm also going to prescribe you some medication to help with your edema. i'm going to prescribe you some furosemide 20 milligrams once a day. i want you to take that for the next 3 days. i also want you to follow up with me in 3 months. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's talk a little bit about your lifestyle. do you have any hobbies or activities that you enjoy?
[patient] yes, i like to watch football.
[doctor] okay, that's great. do you have a favorite team?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay, and do you have a favorite player?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay, well let's talk a little bit about your diet. i want you to try to watch your salt intake and increase your potassium intake. i'm also going to refer you to a nutritionist to help you with that. do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's talk a little bit about your follow-up. i want you to follow up with me in 3 months. i also want you to call me if you have any problems or if you gain 3 pounds in 2 days. do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's review your medications again. you're taking bumex 2 milligrams once a day, cozaar 100 milligrams a day, and norvasc 5 milligrams once a day. are you taking those as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any questions about your medications?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's review your medical history again. i see that you have a history of hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease. do you have any questions about your medical history?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's review your medical plan again. i want you to continue taking your medications as prescribed. i also want you to follow up with me in 3 months. do you have any questions about your medical plan?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well it was nice seeing you today. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well let's go ahead and schedule that follow-up appointment for 3 months from today. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, and do you have any questions for me before you go?
[patient] no, i don't have any questions.
[doctor] okay, well it was nice seeing you today. take care of yourself.
[patient] you too, doctor.
[doctor] okay, bye.
[patient] bye. }}<|eot_id|>
