dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey gregory how are you today
[patient] i'm doing good thanks doc i'm doing good
[doctor] good hey so i know you know you came in here for your ankle
[patient] yeah
[doctor] hey so i know you came in here for your ankle i'm looking at your chart here so i know that you slipped and fell on the ice taking out the trash and you were unable to ambulate at the time of injury and a friend had to help you up and then you iced and elevated it throughout the night and then you've been taking ibuprofen for the pain and that's helped you out some but you're still limping so can you tell me a little bit about your ankle injury
[patient] yeah so i was just taking out the trash and i slipped and fell on the ice and i was unable to get up and a friend had to help me up and then i just iced and elevated it and took some ibuprofen and that's helped it out some
[doctor] okay and can you tell me a little bit about your pain have you had any numbness in your foot
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and any other previous injuries to your right ankle
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and do you play any sports
[patient] i play soccer
[doctor] okay
[patient] yeah i play for the community soccer league
[doctor] okay so you're very active so i'm gon na go ahead and take a look at your ankle so i'm gon na start with your vitals and your vitals look good and then i'm gon na do a quick physical exam and i'm gon na take a look at your ankle so your capillary refill is less than three seconds with a strong dorsalis pedis pulse and your sensation is intact to light touch and i do appreciate some ecchymosis over the lateral malleolus and there is some swelling over the lateral malleolus and there's tenderness to palpation anterolaterally in the soft tissue and no laxity on anterior drawer and inversion stress and no bony tenderness on palpation of the foot and neurovascular intact so i'm gon na go ahead and take a look at your x-rays and i'm gon na show them to you so i don't see any evidence of fracture on your x-rays so i think you sustained a right ankle sprain so i'm gon na go ahead and give you a diagnosis of a right ankle sprain and i'm gon na recommend that you keep your right lower extremity elevated especially when you're seated and you can continue to ice your right ankle and i'm gon na provide you with an aircast to help stabilize your ankle and you're gon na be able to use crutches for the next one to two days and then you can start weight-bearing as tolerated and i'm gon na recommend that you take some ibuprofen as needed for pain and i think you should see significant improvement in your symptoms over the next two weeks and i want you to follow up with me in two weeks to see how you're doing and i'll be able to determine your return to play date and if you have any questions or concerns before you go i'm happy to answer them
[patient] okay
[doctor] so i'm gon na go ahead and give you a prescription for some ibuprofen and i'm gon na give you a prescription for the aircast and i'm gon na go ahead and give you a referral to physical therapy if you need it and i'll see you in two weeks okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay
[patient] alright
[doctor] alright
[patient] thanks doc
[doctor] you're welcome }}<|eot_id|>
