dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well, thanks. i'm here for my annual checkup.
[doctor] great. so, i see that you're here for your annual checkup. i'm doctor, smith, and i'll be taking care of you today. so, can you tell me a little bit about your medical history? have you had any problems?
[patient] i don't think so. i mean, i get sick every now and then, but nothing too serious.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about your family history. do you have any family members with any chronic diseases?
[patient] well, my cousin died of a heart attack when he was in his 40's, but i don't know if that counts.
[doctor] okay. that does count. let's talk about your lifestyle. do you smoke?
[patient] no, i don't smoke.
[doctor] okay. do you have any other vices like drinking or anything like that?
[patient] no, i don't really drink.
[doctor] okay. do you exercise regularly?
[patient] i try to get outside and ride my bike on the trails.
[doctor] that's great. that's good exercise. have you had any problems with your blood pressure or cholesterol in the past?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, let's take a look at your vital signs. your blood pressure looks good. i'm going to go ahead and do a physical exam on you. so, i'm just going to listen to your heart and lungs. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, your heart and lungs sound good. i'm not hearing any abnormal sounds. i'm also going to check your abdomen. your abdomen is normal. i'm not feeling any masses or anything like that. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm going to go ahead and order some tests. i'm going to order a full cholesterol panel and a hemoglobin a1c. i'm also going to order a cmp and a thyroid study and a liver panel. i'm going to check your thyroid function and your liver function to make sure everything is normal. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. i'm also going to order a genetic test to see if you have a genetic predisposition to high cholesterol. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk about your diet. what do you eat?
[patient] i eat a pretty balanced diet, i think.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk about your diet a little bit. i'm going to recommend that you follow a diet that is low in saturated fats and sugars. you can try to eat more fruits and vegetables and whole grains. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'm also going to recommend that you exercise more. you can try to get outside and ride your bike more often or go for a walk.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk about your cholesterol level. your cholesterol level is a little bit high. it's at 210. i'm going to put you on a statin to help lower your cholesterol. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'm also going to recommend that you follow up with me in 3 to 6 months to check your cholesterol level again. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'm going to give you a referral to a nutritionist. they can help you with your diet and exercise plan. okay?
