dialogue is: {{ [doctor] okay, so, uh, so here's what i've got on you. you're a 56 year old female, you've been here for chest pain on exertion. so i know you've had some chest pain, and you're here today because you've been having some chest pain. and you're worried about it. so i'm just gon na go through your history with you and we'll go from there. okay? so you've had diabetes type 2, and you've been doing well with that. you're taking metformin 500 milligrams twice a day. is that correct? and you've had that for a while now? yeah, i've been taking that for a while. okay. and you've had high blood pressure, but you've not been formally diagnosed with hypertension, but your blood pressures have been trending high. and have you been taking any medication for that? no, i have not. okay. and then you've got a family history of heart disease. okay. so you've had chest pain. so you've had chest pain on exertion, and you've been having it for a while now, and it's been bothering you. okay? so, uh, so you've been having chest pain. and you've been taking metformin for your diabetes, and you've been taking that for a while now. and you've had some high blood pressure, but you've not been formally diagnosed with hypertension, but your blood pressures have been trending high. and you've got a family history of heart disease. okay. so, uh, so let's talk about your review of systems. so, uh, do you have any diaphoresis or clamminess? no, i do not. okay. do you have any chest pain? yes, i do. okay. do you have any shortness of breath? no, i do not. okay. do you have any nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea? no, i do not. okay. so, uh, let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so, uh, your neck exam is unremarkable. you do not have any jugular venous distention, swelling, or carotid bruits. okay? your respiratory exam is also unremarkable. your lungs are clear bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. okay? your cardiovascular exam, you do have a 2 over 6 systolic ejection murmur, otherwise your heart rate and rhythm are normal. you do not have any murmurs, gallops, or rubs. your pulses are equal. okay? your abdominal exam is also unremarkable. you do not have any masses or tenderness. your abdomen is soft, and you do not have any guarding. and your musculoskeletal exam, you do have 1 plus nonpitting edema in your ankles. you do not have any calf tenderness. okay? so, uh, let's talk about the results. so, uh, i've reviewed your ecg, and it's unremarkable. your hemoglobin a1c was 7, okay? and then let's talk about my assessment and plan. so, uh, i think your chest pain is likely unstable angina. i know you've had some chest pain on exertion, and i think you might have some sort of blockage causing that pain. so, uh, i want you to take a sublingual nitroglycerin, and i want you to go to the emergency department if that's not effective after about 5 minutes. okay? and then, uh, i'm gon na have you start a regimen of baby aspirin at 81 milligrams a day. i've sent in a prescription for that today. i'm also gon na have you start taking nitroglycerin up to 3 tablets every 5 minutes as needed. and then, uh, i want you to follow up with cardiology for further evaluation. okay? and then, uh, for your diabetes, i think you're doing well on your current regimen. i want you to keep your appointment with ophthalmology for evaluation of diabetic retinopathy. i'm gon na put in an order for a repeat hemoglobin a1c to check for any needed medication adjustments. you're gon na continue with metformin 500 milligrams twice a day, and i want you to continue with dietary modifications. okay? and then, uh, for your hypertension, i think you're due for some adjustments. i want you to monitor your blood pressures at home over the next 2 weeks and report them to me via my chart. and then i'm gon na put you on hydrochlorothiazide at a low dose. okay? so, uh, do you have any questions for me? no, i do not. okay. so, uh, i'm gon na see you in 2 weeks. okay? }}<|eot_id|>
