dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. so, i know that you came in for a follow up of your chronic problem. can you tell me a little bit about what's going on?
[patient] yeah, my osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little bit lately, and i just wanted to talk about that, primarily in my elbows. i've been sitting at the computer more in the office, so i'm not sure if it's just from sitting there all day. my right elbow bothers me more than my left elbow, but i'm primarily typing all day versus writing.
[doctor] okay. and any other joint pain?
[patient] no, just the elbows.
[doctor] okay. and any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] occasional numbness and tingling, but i just shake out my arms to relieve it.
[doctor] okay. and i know that you have a history of gout. when was your last episode of gout?
[patient] that was about three months ago.
[doctor] okay. and what happened?
[patient] i had some inflammation in my toe at that time.
[doctor] okay. and any other issues with that?
[patient] no, nothing else.
[doctor] okay. and the medication that we gave you helped with that, and you haven't seen a flare up since?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and i know that you have psoriasis. how's that been going?
[patient] it's been under control. it'sn't been a major problem for me.
[doctor] okay. and are you still taking the colchicine?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking it twice a day?
[patient] i take it twice a day as needed for flare-ups.
