dialogue is: {{ [doctor] okay christina it's good to see you today so i know you were here for the first time so i'm gon na go ahead and tell you what i'm gon na be doing i'm gon na be recording this encounter and i'll give you a copy of the note i'll give you a copy of the note after we're done okay so christina you're a 77 year old female here for the evaluation of a non healing right foot ulcer so can you tell me a little bit about your ulcer so i know that it started about a year ago and i know that you were seen by your primary care physician and they put you on keflex so can you tell me a little bit about what happened and how you've been doing since then
[patient] okay yeah so it started as a blister and then i picked at it and then it turned red and then it just got bigger and bigger and then i saw my doctor and she put me on keflex and that helped a little bit but it still hasn't gone away
[doctor] okay and when was the last time you were on the keflex
[patient] five months ago
[doctor] okay and do you have any pain with it or is it just there
[patient] no pain
[doctor] okay and are you having any difficulty walking or moving your foot
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any change in sensation in your foot
[patient] yes i have yeah i have less sensation in my foot
[doctor] okay and is there any drainage from the ulcer
[patient] yes there is
[doctor] okay and have you been wearing your regular shoes
[patient] yes i have
[doctor] okay and how about your diabetes i know you have type two diabetes how have your sugars been running
[patient] my sugars have been running better than they were but they're still in the two hundreds
[doctor] okay and i know that you have some neuropathy with that and that's why you're here today so how have you been doing with that
[patient] i'm doing okay
[doctor] okay and then your last hemoglobin a1c was ten
[patient] yes that's right
[doctor] okay so let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam of your right foot so i'm gon na go ahead and examine your right foot and i do see a one centimeter by two centimeter wound on the dorsal aspect of the lateral right foot just proximal to the fifth mtp joint and i do see some yellow slough that is present with minimal granulation tissue there is no surrounding erythema or cellulitis there is no evidence of fluid collection i don't see necrosis no odor no bony exposure and there is no pain to palpation of the foot so i wan na go ahead and look at the x-ray of your foot so i'm looking at the x-ray of your right foot today and i don't see any evidence of osteomyelitis so that's good news and i do wan na go ahead and recommend that we get an ankle brachial index done to determine your blood supply to see if we can heal this wound so i'm gon na go ahead and recommend that we do a debridement in the office today and i'll give you a surgical shoe to put on your foot to provide increased support and i'll also prescribe you some collagenase ointment to apply to your wound one time per day and cover it with a sterile dressing and i'll have you continue that until we see the ulcer decrease in size and then we'll go from there so what do you think
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay so i wan na go ahead and schedule you to come back in two weeks to check on your progress okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] alright so if you have any questions for me just let me know and i'll be happy to answer them otherwise i'll see you in two weeks
[patient] okay
[doctor] alright }}<|eot_id|>
