dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi susan how are you
[patient] i'm doing well thanks how are you
[doctor] i'm doing well so i know that you're here for a high blood pressure check
[patient] yeah that's right
[doctor] okay so i know that you've been struggling with that in the past but it seems like it's out of control recently how are you doing with that
[patient] yeah i've been having a lot of headaches and my blood pressure at home has been over 150 so i'm a little concerned about it
[doctor] okay so you've been taking your norvasc 10 mg daily
[patient] yes i have
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any chest pain or shortness of breath
[patient] no chest pain no shortness of breath
[doctor] okay so let's talk a little bit about your medical history i know that you had a kidney transplant a few years ago how are you doing with that
[patient] i'm doing well i'm taking all of my immunosuppression medication and everything is going well
[doctor] okay so let's do a quick review of systems here so you don't have any chest pain or shortness of breath
[patient] no
[doctor] any shortness of breath
[patient] no
[doctor] any headaches
[patient] yes i've had some headaches
[doctor] okay so let's do a quick physical exam here so on your physical exam you're in no apparent distress your neck is supple without any thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally no wheezes rales or rhonchi your heart has a two over six systolic ejection murmur on your musculoskeletal exam you don't have any edema and your skin exam shows a scar on your left flank from your kidney transplant and that's healed so let's look at some of your lab results here so your creatinine is normal and your ecg is normal so let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan for you so for your first problem of hypertension i think that you do need to get your blood pressure under better control i'm gon na order a lipid panel and metabolic panel to see where you are with your cholesterol and your blood sugar levels and i'm gon na start you on carvedilol 25 milligrams twice a day to help bring your blood pressure down
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay and for your second problem of status post kidney transplant i think you're doing well and your kidney function is stable so we will continue your current medications and i will see you back in about six weeks and we will check your blood pressure again and see how you're doing
[patient] okay that sounds good
