dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm a little tired.
[doctor] okay. so i know we saw you last time for that insect bite and you had a lyme titer done. and it was positive. how are you feeling?
[patient] i've been feeling really tired. and i've had some swollen elbow joints and body aches. and i've had a rash. it's like a bullseye on my side.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any fever?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been eating?
[patient] not much. i've just been eating crackers and things like that.
[doctor] okay. and how's your diabetes been? how's your blood sugar been?
[patient] it's been okay. it's been a little high sometimes. and sometimes a little low. but nothing too out of range.
[doctor] okay. and how's your hypertension? how's your blood pressure been?
[patient] it's been good. i've been monitoring it at home.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any abdominal pain or diarrhea?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. so let's do a quick physical exam. so on your abdomen, it's a little warm to the touch, but it's not tender to palpation. and on your elbows, there's swelling and pain to palpation of the joints bilaterally. and on your skin, i see a small bullseye rash on the left abdominal quadrant. and on your white blood cell count, it's within normal limits. all the other labs are normal as well. so for your first problem, the new diagnosis of lyme disease. i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe you doxycycline 100 milligrams twice a day for three weeks. i'm also gon na touch base with an infectious disease doctor to make sure that we're not missing anything else. and i want to see you back in one week for follow-up. for your second problem, your hypertension. it sounds like it's been well-controlled based on your home monitoring. you've been compliant with dietary modifications, limiting your sodium intake. i'm gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel. you can continue to take your lisinopril 10 milligrams a day. and i'll refill that for you today. for your third problem, your diabetes type two. it sounds like you've been compliant with metformin. you've been noticing some intermittent elevations of your blood glucose levels. i'm gon na go ahead and order a hemoglobin a1c to make sure we're not needing to make any medication changes. and then i'll see you back in a couple weeks to check on how you're doing.
[patient] okay. sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and i'll see you in a couple weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
