[doctor] good good so i know that you're here for your annual exam today i see that you had a right carpal tunnel release about two years ago how are you doing with that
[patient] i'm doing well i mean i'm not really feeling any numbness or tingling in my hand
[doctor] okay good and how about your depression how are you doing with that
[patient] i'm doing well i've been going to therapy every week and i've been taking my medication as prescribed
[doctor] okay good and how's the therapy going
[patient] it's going well it's been helpful
[doctor] okay good and how about your sleep how are you sleeping
[patient] i'm sleeping well i'm getting about eight hours a night
[doctor] okay good and are you checking your blood pressure at home
[patient] yes i am i've been checking it at home and my blood pressure has been fluctuating a little bit
[doctor] okay and what kind of fluctuations are you seeing
[patient] it's just that it's not been normal in the last couple of weeks
[doctor] okay and are you taking your lisinopril as prescribed
[patient] yes i am
[doctor] okay good and how about your diet has that changed at all
[patient] a little bit it's been all over the place
[doctor] okay and are you working more hours
[patient] yeah i've been working a lot more hours
[doctor] okay and are you having any headaches
[patient] a little bit but i think it's just because i've been on the computer a lot
[doctor] okay and any other symptoms
[patient] no i'm good
[doctor] okay good and let's do a quick physical exam here on your neck is that supple
[patient] yeah
[doctor] and do you have any thyroid enlargement
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and your lungs are clear to auscultation
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay and your heart sounds good regular rate and rhythm no murmurs gallops or rubs and no extra heart sounds
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay and your grip strength is equal and strong
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay and any numbness or tingling in your hands or fingers
[patient] no
[doctor] okay good and let's look at your vitals here and i see that your blood pressure is a little elevated so i'm gon na go ahead and order some labs and we'll take a look at those and i'm gon na increase your lisinopril to ten milligrams once a day
[patient] okay
[doctor] and i want you to continue to monitor that at home and we'll follow up in a month and i want you to continue with your current regimen for your depression and i want you to continue to go to therapy
[patient] okay
[doctor] and how does that sound
[patient] that sounds good
[doctor] okay good and any questions for me
[patient] no i don't think so
[doctor] okay good well you have a great day
[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>
