dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, good morning, jordan, how are you doing today?
[patient] good morning, good to see you.
[doctor] good to see you as well. i know you were in the emergency room last month for some palpitations and high blood pressure. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've been trying to monitor my blood pressure at home and i've been doing okay with it.
[doctor] okay. and i know you were in the emergency room for palpitations and high blood pressure. do you remember what happened?
[patient] yeah, i do. i had a panic attack and i had a lot of anxiety and my heart was racing.
[doctor] okay. and you said you had a lot of anxiety?
[patient] yeah, i did.
[doctor] okay. and do you think it was just the anxiety or was it the coffee you had in the morning?
[patient] i think it was a combination of both.
[doctor] okay. and how many cups of coffee did you have?
[patient] i had a few cups.
[doctor] okay. and was it an empty stomach?
[patient] yeah, it was an empty stomach.
[doctor] okay. all right. and have you had any episodes of palpitations since then?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms since then?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and how's your blood pressure been since then?
[patient] it's been a little high. i've been monitoring it at home and it's been running around 146 to 155.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any family history of high blood pressure?
[patient] yeah, several family members have it.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing to help control your blood pressure?
[patient] i've been monitoring it at home and i've been trying to cut back on my salt intake.
[doctor] okay. and how's that going?
[patient] it's been going well. i've been doing pretty good with it.
[doctor] okay. and have you been exercising?
[patient] yeah, i try to walk on my treadmill as often as i can.
[doctor] okay. all right. and i know you've been seeing your new primary care doctor and she started you on a new medication. what's the name of that medication?
[patient] benicar.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing on that?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've been taking it for about a month now.
[doctor] okay. and any side effects?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay. all right. and i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam. i'm gon na call out some of my findings as i do the exam. so, your heart rate is normal, your rhythm is regular, your s2 is normal, your heart sounds are normal, and your pulses are normal. your lungs are clear to auscultation, bilaterally. your abdomen is non-tender. and there's no edema. i'm gon na go ahead and order some labs. i'm gon na order a basic metabolic panel. i'm gon na check your electrolytes, your kidney function, and your thyroid function. i also want to check your thyroid function. i know you had that done in march, but i want to make sure that everything is okay.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i wan na go ahead and talk to you about my assessment and plan. so, your blood pressure is a little high. it's resistant to the medications that we've been using. we've tried maxing out the doses of the three medications that you're on. and i think we need to try some other medications to help control your blood pressure. i'm gon na go ahead and add spironolactone. i want you to continue with the benicar and the amlodipine. i want you to take the spironolactone once a day. and i want you to monitor your potassium levels. i want you to come back and see me in two weeks. and we're gon na check your blood pressure and your basic metabolic panel. i also want you to reduce your sodium intake. i want you to limit it to 1500 to 2000 milligrams per day. i want you to follow the dash diet. i'm gon na give you some materials. i want you to try to meet at least 30 minutes of walking most days.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. i'm gon na go ahead and order the labs. i'm gon na go ahead and order the spironolactone. and i'll talk to you in two weeks.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i'll talk to you in two weeks. and we'll see how you're doing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. all right. i'll talk to you in two weeks. i'll see you then.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. bye.
[patient] bye.
 }}<|eot_id|>
