dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, brittany, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm a little bit better than i was last time i came in.
[doctor] okay. so, how's your symptoms been?
[patient] it's been better. i've been having a lot of stress at work, so it's been kind of a little bit worse.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, we had discussed that you had irritable bowel syndrome. so, what's been going on?
[patient] yeah, so i've been having some cramps and sharp pains in my stomach, and sometimes i feel nauseous, and i've been having some diarrhea.
[doctor] okay. so, what's been causing those symptoms? have you noticed anything that triggers it?
[patient] well, i had some shrimp the other day, and it made me have both upper and lower abdominal pain and bloating.
[doctor] okay. and then, have you noticed any other foods that make your symptoms worse?
[patient] yeah, when i eat chicken alfredo, i get diarrhea.
[doctor] okay. and then, what about drinking?
[patient] i don't think it makes a difference.
[doctor] okay. how many drinks do you have a week?
[patient] um, i don't know. i don't really count them. i have like, two drinks when i'm out of either tequila or brown liquor. occasionally, i'll have a martini.
[doctor] okay. and then, what about, like, heavy foods or fried foods?
[patient] i try to avoid them. but, i had fried chicken today and it didn't bother me.
[doctor] okay. and then, what about sodas? do you drink a lot of soda?
[patient] no, i don't drink soda.
[doctor] okay. and then, what about your bowel movements? how often do you go?
[patient] i go like, two to three times a day.
[doctor] okay. and are they formed or are they loose?
[patient] they're formed.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about your symptoms. so, you're having some cramps and sharp pains. have you noticed any nausea?
[patient] yeah, i have.
[doctor] okay. and then, you're having some diarrhea. are you having any vomiting?
[patient] sometimes.
[doctor] okay. and then, what about constipation?
[patient] no, i don't have constipation.
[doctor] okay. so, let's do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na listen to your lungs. (pause) your lungs sound clear. i'm gon na listen to your heart. your heart sounds good. i'm gon na do a quick abdominal exam. (pause) your abdomen is soft. it's not tender. i don't feel any masses or organomegaly. your bowel sounds are normal.
