dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, jeremy. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm a little stiff today. i've been having some back problems.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about what's going on with your back. how long have you been having this problem?
[patient] um, it started about four months ago. i was moving some boxes out of my son's college dorm. and i was lifting and moving some boxes and i felt a little bit of tingling in my right toes. and then after about an hour, that went away. but after that, i felt like i couldn't support my upper body weight. and i've been having some weakness in my legs when i'm carrying heavy objects. and then sometimes when i turn a certain way or roll over in my sleep, i get a sharp pain in my lower back. but it goes away after i reposition myself.
[doctor] okay. so it's kind of like a sharp pain that you feel in your lower back?
[patient] yeah, that's right.
[doctor] okay. and have you been able to do anything to help with the pain?
[patient] i've been taking tylenol and ibuprofen. and i've been using heat and ice. but it really doesn't seem to help.
[doctor] okay. and have you tried anything else?
[patient] i tried physical therapy at my gym. but that didn't really help.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms like fever or chills or anything like that?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any problems with your bladder or your bowels?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other surgeries in the past?
[patient] yeah, i had a total knee replacement about two years ago.
[doctor] okay. and how's that doing?
[patient] it's doing really well. i'd say it's about 95% better.
