dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, john. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm a little worried about my shortness of breath and the blood i've been coughing up.
[doctor] okay. let's take a deep breath together. i know this can be really scary. can you tell me more about your shortness of breath and the blood?
[patient] yeah. i just started feeling short of breath a couple of weeks ago and it's just been getting progressively worse. and then i've been coughing up blood. it's pretty scary.
[doctor] okay. have you had any fever?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and any bleeding from your gums?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and any pain in your joints?
[patient] yeah, my knee has been hurting me for a while now.
[doctor] okay. and any pain in your legs?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any bruising?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and can you tell me a little bit about your medical history? what are you being treated for?
[patient] i'm being treated for diabetes and high blood pressure and asthma.
[doctor] okay. and what medications are you taking for those?
[patient] i'm taking metformin and norvasc.
[doctor] okay. and how's your diabetes been controlled?
[patient] it's been up and down. i've been having some trouble with it.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood pressure?
[patient] it's been running a little low.
[doctor] okay. and your asthma?
[patient] it's been okay.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na listen to your lungs and your heart and just check your blood pressure. okay?
[patient] okay.
