dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. chavez. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing well. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. good to see you. so i know you were in the hospital for some issues. can you tell me a little bit about what happened?
[patient] so, i was having chest pain, and i was rushed to the hospital. and then they told me that i had a heart attack. i had a heart attack.
[doctor] okay. so, i know you had an inferior heart attack. how are you doing now? are you having any chest pain?
[patient] no, i'm not having any chest pain. but my legs have been swollen.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any shortness of breath?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. so, let's take a look at your vitals. and everything looks good. your blood pressure is a little bit high, but that's to be expected. i'm going to go ahead and order some labs to see how you're doing. and then i'm going to go ahead and do a physical exam. so, i'm just gon na call out some of my findings as i go along. so, on your physical exam, your neck is normal. your heart is normal. you do have a 3/6 systolic ejection murmur at the left base. and your lower extremities have 1+ pitting edema. so, i know that you had a heart attack. and i know that you had some blood work done in the hospital. i know that you had an ekg and an echocardiogram. and i know that they put a stent in your heart. and i know that you had some medication changes. so, let's talk a little bit about your heart. so, your heart attack was an inferior heart attack. and that's because one of the arteries that brings blood to your heart got blocked. and you had some damage to that muscle. and so, i know that you had an echocardiogram. and that showed that your heart is functioning at about 35% of its normal function. and that's because of the damage that you had. but the good news is that you were able to get treated in a timely manner. and that's very important. so, i'm expecting that that muscle is just stunned and that it will get better over time.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? and then, i know that you're currently on a lot of medications. so, let's talk a little bit about those. so, you're on aspirin, brilinta, lipitor, toprol, lisinopril, and metformin. and i know that you're taking those medications as prescribed. and i know that you're doing well with that. so, let's talk a little bit about your heart failure. so, you're retaining a lot of fluid. and that's why your legs are swollen. and so, i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe some medications to help with that. so, i'm gon na prescribe lasix 40 mg once a day. and i'm gon na add aldactone 12.5 mg daily. and then, i'm gon na order some lab work. and then, i'm gon na order a repeat echo in about two months to see how you're doing. and then, let's talk a little bit about your hypertension. so, your blood pressure is well controlled. and that's because of your lisinopril. and i know that you're doing well with that. so, let's talk a little bit about your diabetes. so, your blood sugars are stable. and that's because of your metformin. and i know that you're doing well with that. so, let's talk a little bit about your nutrition. so, i know that you're eating a lot of preserved meats. and i know that that's not good for your heart. so, i'm gon na go ahead and refer you to nutrition counseling. and then, let's talk a little bit about your exercise. so, i know that you're not doing as much exercise as you would like. and that's because of your heart. so, i'm gon na go ahead and refer you to cardiac rehab. and then, i'm gon na encourage you to start walking more. and then, let's talk a little bit about your medication regimen. so, i know that you're doing well with your medications. but i'm gon na go ahead and remind you to take them as prescribed. and then, let's talk a little bit about your follow-up. so, i know that you have a follow-up appointment with me in two weeks. and then, i want to see you back in two months to check on your progress. and then, let's talk a little bit about your education. so, i know that you're doing well with your medications. but i'm gon na go ahead and educate you on how to use your aldactone and your lasix. and then, let's talk a little bit about your blood pressure. so, i know that your blood pressure is well controlled. and that's because of your lisinopril. and i know that you're doing well with that. so, let's talk a little bit about your diet. so, i know that you're eating a lot of preserved meats. and i know that that's not good for your heart. so, i'm gon na go ahead and refer you to nutrition counseling. and then, let's talk a little bit about your exercise. so, i know that you're not doing as much exercise as you would like. and that's because of your heart. so, i'm gon na go ahead and refer you to cardiac rehab. and then, i'm gon na encourage you to start walking more. so, i think that's all for today. do you have any questions for me?
