dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. thanks.
[doctor] great. so, what brings you in today?
[patient] i have some elbow pain. it's been bothering me for a while.
[doctor] okay. okay. so, you're having some elbow pain?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. so, is that on your right elbow or your left?
[patient] it's more on my right elbow.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, can you tell me a little bit about what you've been doing to cause that elbow pain?
[patient] i've been sitting at the computer a lot more at the office, so i'm not sure if it's just from sitting in the same position all day.
[doctor] okay. okay. and have you been doing any other activities that might cause that pain?
[patient] no, just sitting at the computer.
[doctor] okay. all right. and how about any other joints? any other pain?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and what about your psoriasis? is that still under control?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and how about your gout? have you had any flare ups recently?
[patient] i had a flare up about three months ago.
[doctor] okay. and how did you treat that?
[patient] i was given some medication and it helped.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other issues with gout since then?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam. and i'm gon na listen to your heart and lungs, and i'm gon na do a quick abdominal exam. and i'm gon na check your joints.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i don't feel anything unusual with your heart and lungs. and your abdomen is soft. and i don't see any swelling in your legs. and i'm gon na check your right elbow. i don't see any swelling, but i do feel some tenderness to the olecranon bursa. and i don't see any redness or warmth. i do feel some pain with pronation and supination. and i do feel some pain with flexion and extension of your right arm.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i think i'm gon na order an x-ray of your right elbow. i think you might have some osteoarthritis. i'm gon na prescribe you some meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for the pain and swelling. and we'll also continue you on the colchicine for your gout. and we'll continue the steroid cream for your psoriasis.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, that's all.
[doctor] okay. all right. and do you understand what we're gon na do?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. all right. i'll go ahead and order those tests and we'll get you set up with the medication.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, sounds good. }}<|eot_id|>
