dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, beverly. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. i've been working at a bakery this summer.
[doctor] okay, good. i've heard you're working at a bakery. how's that going?
[patient] it's been good. i've been trying to improve my diet by removing some of the sweets.
[doctor] okay, well, that's great. so, how have you been doing with your diabetes?
[patient] it's been a little up and down. my blood sugars have been fluctuating a little bit.
[doctor] okay, have you been taking your medication?
[patient] yes, i have. i've been taking my metformin twice a day and i haven't missed any doses.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood pressure? how's that been?
[patient] it's been good, thank you.
[doctor] okay, that's great. and how about your sleep? how's that been?
[patient] it's been good. i've been sleeping well.
[doctor] okay, that's good. and have you been having any thoughts of self-harm or suicidal ideations?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay, that's good. all right, so let's do a quick physical exam. (pause) your grip strength is equal bilaterally. your neurologic exam is intact. your neck is supple without any thyroid enlargement or lymph nodes. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. you do have a grade two out of six systolic ejection fraction murmur. you do not have any extra heart sounds. your pulses are good. all right, so let's talk a little bit about your labs. your hemoglobin a1c was elevated.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] yeah, your hemoglobin a1c was 8.5.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so we'll need to work on getting that down. have you had a chance to look at your fasting blood glucose levels?
[patient] not recently, no.
[doctor] okay. i think it would be helpful for you to check those every morning and call them in about two weeks. we can discuss further treatment options at that time. have you been taking your lisinopril?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay, good. and how's that been working for you?
[patient] it's been good.
[doctor] okay. well, i think we'll continue that for now. and then for your diabetes, we'll continue the metformin twice a day. i want you to try to improve your diet and reduce your sweets. and we'll follow up in about two months and discuss further treatment options. does that sound good to you?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, good. well, i think we're all set. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay, good. well, take care of yourself.
[patient] thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
