dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi anna. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i've been having some elbow pain.
[doctor] okay. i'm anna morris. i'm a nurse practitioner. i'm here to help you with your elbow pain. can you tell me a little bit about what's going on with your elbow?
[patient] yeah, i've been having some pain in my left elbow. it's been really stiff and painful. i've been sitting at my desk all day for work and my elbows are bent. after work it's really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. i've also noticed some swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.
[doctor] okay. that sounds really painful. do you have any fever or chills?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] no, nothing like that. i do have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any weakness in your arm?
[patient] yeah, i have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant.
[doctor] okay. all right. and have you noticed any pain in your chest?
[patient] no, i don't have any chest pain.
[doctor] okay. all right. have you noticed any shortness of breath?
[patient] no, i don't have any shortness of breath.
[doctor] okay. have you had any nausea or vomiting?
[patient] no, i don't have any nausea or vomiting.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any abdominal pain?
[patient] no, i don't have any abdominal pain.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any nasal congestion?
[patient] yeah, i have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.
[doctor] okay. all right. have you had any recent seizures?
[patient] no, i haven't had any recent seizures. my last seizure was a year ago.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications?
[patient] i'm taking keppra for my seizures.
[doctor] okay. all right. and are you taking any other medications?
[patient] i'm also taking protonix for my stomach.
[doctor] okay. all right. all right. let's do a physical exam. so on physical exam, your left elbow reveals erythema and edema. there is pain to palpation of the left olecranon. there is warmth to palpation. there is pain with flexion and extension. there is a palpable left radial pulse.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. so on x-ray of your left arm, we did not see any evidence of elbow fracture.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and on endoscopy, you had an episode of gastritis.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. so i think you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so i'm gon na put you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you may also ice the area.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and i'm gon na continue you on your keppra 500 milligrams twice a day. i'm gon na refill that for you today.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and i think you're doing well with your therapy. i'm gon na start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once a day. i want you to continue that. and i'm gon na continue you on protonix 40 milligrams once a day before meals.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and how's your depression going?
[patient] it's been good. i've been doing alright.
[doctor] okay. all right. any suicidal or homicidal ideations?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. all right. any other questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] all right. well, let's get you checked out. and i'll have my nurse come in and get you all checked out. and then we'll get you scheduled for a follow-up.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. sounds good.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. i'll see you in a little bit. }}<|eot_id|>
