dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, susan how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well, thank you.
[doctor] good. so i understand that you're here today for a high blood pressure check. have you been having any issues?
[patient] i've always struggled with high blood pressure, but it seems out of control recently. i've been taking norvasc 10 mg daily. my blood pressure at home has been over 150.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any symptoms like headaches or chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] i've had some headaches, but i'm not sure if it's due to stress at work or my high blood pressure. i don't have any chest pain or shortness of breath.
[doctor] okay. and how have you been doing with your kidney transplant? is everything going well?
[patient] yeah, everything is going well. i'm taking all of my immunosuppression medication.
[doctor] good. so let's do a quick review of your systems. have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no chest pain or shortness of breath.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any shortness of breath?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any headaches?
[patient] yes, headaches.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any neurological symptoms?
[patient] yes, headaches.
[doctor] okay. let's do a quick physical exam. your vital signs look good. your heart exam is normal, no murmurs. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. you do have a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur. your abdomen is soft and non-tender. you do have a scar on your left flank from your kidney transplant, which is healed. everything else is normal on exam.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel and metabolic panel. and i'm gon na put you on carvedilol 25 mg twice a day to help bring your blood pressure down. does that sound good to you?
[patient] that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and i know that you're doing well with your kidney transplant. i'm gon na continue your current medications. i will order a creatinine level to make sure your kidney function is stable. and i'll order an ekg to make sure everything is okay with your heart.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] any questions for me?
[patient] no questions.
[doctor] okay. i will have my nurse come in and give you the prescriptions. and we'll get the lab work ordered. do you have any questions?
[patient] no questions.
[doctor] okay. all right, i'll see you in a few minutes. my nurse will be in shortly to give you the prescriptions and answer any other questions you may have. }}<|eot_id|>
