dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, ms. lee. how are you?
[patient] good morning. i'm doing alright.
[doctor] yeah. how's your back feeling?
[patient] it's been really sore.
[doctor] okay. so tell me a little bit about what happened. how did you hurt your back?
[patient] well, i was at a birthday party and i was running up the stairs and i ran into the railing and twisted my back. and now it hurts.
[doctor] okay. did you fall or did you just twist it?
[patient] i just twisted it.
[doctor] okay. and how long ago did this happen?
[patient] um, probably like three days ago.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt all the time or is it just when you move?
[patient] it hurts all the time.
[doctor] okay. and is it just in your lower back or does it go down into your legs?
[patient] no, it just stays in my lower back.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any fever or chills?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and are you nauseated?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you taken anything for the pain?
[patient] i've been taking ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. and how many ibuprofen have you taken?
[patient] um, i don't know. a lot.
[doctor] okay. and is that helping?
[patient] it's not really helping.
[doctor] okay. and have you tried ice or heat?
[patient] i've tried heat.
[doctor] okay. and how about lying flat? does that make it hurt?
[patient] yeah, that makes it hurt.
[doctor] okay. and twisting motions?
[patient] yeah, that makes it hurt too.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you stand up?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and is there any numbness or tingling?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any similar problems in the past?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any surgeries?
[patient] i had a lumbar fusion.
[doctor] okay. and how long ago was that?
[patient] um, about 10 years ago.
[doctor] okay. and how has that been doing?
[patient] it's been doing good.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let's go ahead and do a physical exam. (pause) okay, so i'm gon na press on your back. (pause) okay, i'm gon na press on your lower back. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your reflexes. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your sensation. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your straight leg raise. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your range of motion. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your muscle strength. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your muscle tone. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your sensation in your legs. (pause) okay, i'm gon na check your reflexes in your legs. (pause) all right. so i'm gon na look at the x-rays. (pause) okay, so the x-rays show that you do have a prior lumbar fusion. and it looks like your hardware is in good position. there is no evidence of any acute fracture. but i do see some degenerative disc disease in your lower back. so i think you have a lumbar strain. and i think that's what's causing your pain. i think you should continue to take the ibuprofen. i think you should try to avoid lying flat. i think you should try to avoid twisting motions. i think you should try to use ice and heat. and i think you should try to take motrin 800 milligrams 3 times a day with food. and if that doesn't help, then we can discuss other options. okay?
[patient] okay. that sounds good.
[doctor] alright. so i will see you in 2 weeks and we will recheck your back. and if you have any problems before then, please don't hesitate to reach out to me. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] alright, thanks for coming in. }}<|eot_id|>
