dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, hannah, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing well, thanks. i'm just a little nervous about the blood sugar.
[doctor] okay, well, i'm glad you came in. so, you know, you're here for that high blood sugar that you were diagnosed with in the emergency room, is that right?
[patient] yes, i was having some problems, and they said that my blood sugar was really high.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk about that. so, when did you first notice that your blood sugar was high?
[patient] well, i was at my cousin's house, and i just felt really lightheaded, and i was seeing spots in my vision, and i was really dizzy. and then i just collapsed, and i think that's when they called 911.
[doctor] okay. and how are you feeling now?
[patient] i'm feeling a little better, but i'm still a little lightheaded.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about your medical history. you have a history of atrial fibrillation. is that correct?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with that? any issues?
[patient] i've been doing well. i've been taking the metoprolol, and i've been fine.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and what about your acid reflux? how's that been?
[patient] it's been doing well. i've been taking the protonix, and it's been really helpful.
[doctor] okay. great. so, let's talk a little bit about your lifestyle. what do you do for a living?
[patient] i'm a teacher.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of diet do you follow?
[patient] i'm not really following a diet. i eat whatever i want.
[doctor] okay. and do you exercise?
[patient] not as much as i should.
[doctor] okay. and what about your sleep? do you get a good night's sleep?
[patient] i try to, but it's hard with the holidays and everything.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about your family history. is there any diabetes in your family?
[patient] no, not that i know of.
[doctor] okay. and any other medical conditions?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, let's do a quick physical exam. your blood pressure is a little high. your heart rate is a little fast, but your heart sounds good. your lungs are clear. your abdomen is nice and soft. and your thyroid is a little bit enlarged, but it's not tender. and your lower extremities do not have any edema.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm going to order some lab work. we'll do a complete metabolic panel to check your blood sugar levels and your kidney function. and we'll also check your hemoglobin a1c to see how your blood sugar has been over the past few months. and we'll also check your liver enzymes to make sure your liver is functioning properly. and i'm going to start you on metformin 500 milligrams twice a day to help lower your blood sugar levels. i want you to use a glucometer to check your blood sugar levels at home, and we'll go from there.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, any questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll have my nurse come in and get you set up with the metformin, and we'll get you all set up with that glucometer. and i'll also refill your protonix. and i'll have my nurse come in and get you set up with that. and i'll also prescribe you some metoprolol for your atrial fibrillation. and we'll get you all set up with that. and i'll have my nurse come in and get you set up with that. and i'll also give you a referral to a nutritionist to help you with your diet. okay?
[patient] okay, that sounds great.
[doctor] okay, sounds good. well, i'll talk to you soon. thank you.
[patient] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
