dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, janet. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've just been having some joint pain in my knees.
[doctor] mm-hmm. okay. so, um, what's going on with the joint pain? you know, i know you're doing some stair workouts and i'm wondering if that's causing some of the pain.
[patient] yeah, i've been doing stair workouts and i thought it was building muscle on my knees, but i guess it's not.
[doctor] okay. and are you having any pins and needles in your feet or swelling in your legs?
[patient] no, i don't have any of that.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any fever or chills?
[patient] no, i don't have any of those either.
[doctor] okay. and any nausea or vomiting?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and you had a right shoulder rotator cuff repair about two years ago. how's that doing?
[patient] it's doing well.
[doctor] okay, good. and how about your diabetes? are those under control?
[patient] yes, they are.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood pressure? you're taking norvasc 5 mg a day. has that been okay?
[patient] yes, my blood pressure has been fine.
[doctor] okay. and how about any other symptoms? any dizziness or headaches?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. well, let's do a quick physical exam. (pause) okay, so on your physical exam, your neck is supple without any thyromegaly. your heart is regular rate and rhythm. your lungs are clear bilaterally with no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. on your musculoskeletal exam, you have some slight erythema and edema of your left knee. there is a small effusion present. you have decreased flexion and extension of your left knee. your strength in your lower extremities is good.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and let's take a look at your x-rays. (pause) okay, so on your x-rays, there's no fractures, dislocations, or other abnormalities of your left knee.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about your diagnosis and plan. i think you have a left knee strain. we'll order an autoimmune panel for further workup. i'm also going to refer you to physical therapy and prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once daily to help with your pain.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm also concerned about your hypertension. your blood pressure was a little elevated in the office today, but it's been well-controlled on norvasc 5 mg daily based on home monitoring. so, we'll continue your current regimen and home monitoring. we'll also order a lipid profile.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and finally, i'm concerned about your diabetes type ii. your hemoglobin a1c is slightly elevated, but your blood glucose levels have been well-controlled. so, we'll continue your metformin 500 mg twice a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll have my nurse come in and we'll get you all set up with your prescriptions and referrals. okay?
[patient] sounds good.
[doctor] okay. take care.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
