dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, mr. roberts. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well, thank you. i'm glad to be here.
[doctor] good. i'm dr. smith. i've reviewed your history and i noticed that you had a visit to the emergency room in march for palpitations and high blood pressure. how are you doing with that?
[patient] i'm doing well. i've been monitoring my blood pressure at home, and i've been keeping it under control. i've been taking my medication as prescribed.
[doctor] okay. good. can you tell me a little bit about your history with hypertension? have you had it for a long time?
[patient] yes, i've had it for a while. i've been diagnosed for about 10 years now.
[doctor] okay. and how have you been managing it? have you been taking any medications for it?
[patient] yes, i've been taking amlodipine, and i've also been taking benicar hct, which is the new medication that my new primary care physician prescribed.
[doctor] okay. have you been taking those medications as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and how have you been doing with your blood pressure? are you checking it regularly?
[patient] yes, i've been checking it regularly. it's been ranging from 146 to 155.
[doctor] okay. that's good. have you noticed any other symptoms with your blood pressure, such as palpitations?
[patient] yes, i had an episode of palpitations in march.
[doctor] okay. and what do you think caused that?
[patient] i'm not sure. i had consumed several cups of coffee on an empty stomach that morning.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other episodes of palpitations?
[patient] no, not since then.
[doctor] okay. good. and what about your family history? do you have a family history of hypertension?
[patient] yes, several family members have it.
