dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, brittany how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright, i've been having a little bit of stomach issues.
[doctor] okay, so i see that you're back here for follow up for your irritable bowel syndrome. how are you doing?
[patient] i've been doing alright, i've been having some flare ups.
[doctor] okay. so let's talk a little bit about your symptoms. so what's been going on? have you noticed any changes in your symptoms?
[patient] yeah, i've been having some cramps and sharp pains. and sometimes i get diarrhea and nausea.
[doctor] okay. so, what do you think triggers these symptoms? have you noticed anything that makes them worse or better?
[patient] yeah, i think eating certain foods makes it worse. like shrimp and chicken alfredo. but i don't think the alfredo is what's causing it.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any other foods that make it worse or better?
[patient] yeah, like if i eat fried chicken, i don't get symptoms.
[doctor] okay. and what about drinks? do you drink a lot of soda?
[patient] i used to drink a lot of soda but i've stopped.
