[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about your review of systems. so, have you had any problems with your breathing or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you had any chest pain or palpitations?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you had any dizziness or lightheadedness?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you had any changes in your bowel movements?
[patient] yeah, i've been having diarrhea.
[doctor] okay. have you had any abdominal pain?
[patient] yeah, i've been having some cramps and sharp pains.
[doctor] okay. have you had any nausea or vomiting?
[patient] yeah, i've been having some nausea and vomiting.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about your physical exam. so, how are you feeling right now? are you feeling okay?
[patient] yeah, i'm feeling alright.
[doctor] okay. and can you tell me a little bit about your abdomen? is it tender to the touch?
[patient] no, it's not tender.
[doctor] okay. and are you able to feel any masses or organomegaly?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and are your bowel sounds normal?
[patient] yeah, they are.
[doctor] okay. and are your lungs clear to auscultation?
[patient] yeah, they are.
[doctor] okay. and what about your heart? is it regular rate and rhythm?
[patient] yeah, it is.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, i think you have irritable bowel syndrome. i know that you've had some symptoms in the past, but it sounds like they're still going on.
[patient] yeah, they are.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm going to prescribe you some bentyl. this is a medication that can help with some of the cramping and abdominal pain. i want you to take 20 milligrams as needed 30-45 minutes before eating out at a restaurant. this can help with some of the symptoms.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i also want you to start a low dose fiber supplement like citrucel daily. this can help with some of the constipation.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to start probiotics to help with some of the gas and bloating.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to continue with the bentyl 4 times a day. i know you were taking it before, but i want you to continue with it.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to discontinue the reglan and use zofran as needed for nausea.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to avoid greasy fatty foods and alcohol consumption.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to try to reduce your stress and get some better sleeping habits.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm also going to prescribe you a neuromodulator, such as elavil, 25 milligrams at bedtime. this can help with some of the symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i want you to take this at bedtime and see how you do. and then we can adjust the dose as needed.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i want you to follow up with me in one month or sooner if needed. and i also want you to send me a mychart message if you have any side effects or issues with the elavil or if you need to adjust the dose.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay. alright, well, i'll see you in a month or sooner if needed. }}<|eot_id|>
