dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, i guess. i'm a little nervous.
[doctor] okay, well, let's talk about what brings you in today. i understand that you're here for full-spectrum std testing. can you tell me a little bit about what's going on?
[patient] yeah, so i've been having some symptoms. i've been having some discomfort, some discharge, some odor, and some pain on the right side of my vagina. and i just learned that my partner of three years has been having sex with other people for a while, and i want to make sure that i'm okay.
[doctor] okay, so you've had some symptoms and you're concerned because you found out your partner has been having sex with other people. what kind of symptoms are you experiencing?
[patient] yeah, i've had some discomfort, a change in discharge, and an odor in my vaginal region. and the right side of my vagina is starting to become painful but i don't have a fever or chills.
[doctor] okay, have you noticed any changes in the color or consistency of the discharge?
[patient] yeah, i've noticed a change in the odor, color, and consistency of my vaginal discharge last week. and i didn't think much of it until the right side of my vagina became painful and sore and that hasn't gone away.
[doctor] okay, have you had any abnormal pap smears in the past?
[patient] yeah, i had an abnormal pap smear around the age of twenty. but all my pap smears since then, including my most recent one about six months ago, have been normal.
[doctor] okay, all right. well, let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so i'm gon na do a pelvic exam. i'm gon na look at your external genitalia. everything looks normal here. i'm gon na look at your labia majora and labia minora, and everything looks normal. i'm gon na look at your vaginal discharge. your discharge is normal, normal color, normal odor. i'm gon na do a cervical exam. your cervix is normal. your vaginal wall is normal. i don't see any cervical motion tenderness or masses.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm gon na take some swabs for std testing. gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. and then we'll call you with the results of those tests. so, have you had any stds in the past?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order those tests. and we'll call you with the results. and i'll talk to you about what they are and what they mean. and we'll go from there. okay?
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] okay, all right. i'll talk to you soon. }}<|eot_id|>
