[doctor] okay. okay. well, let's do a physical exam. your lower right extremity, your knee is swollen. it's got reduced range of motion. your skin is warm to touch, and it pitts with pressure. i'm gon na go ahead and do a procedure on your knee. i'm gon na do a fluid aspiration and a steroid injection. i'm gon na explain the risks and benefits to you.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] the risks of the steroid injection include, but are not limited to, hypopigmentation, soft tissue atrophy, tendon ruptures, and transient hyperglycemia, among others. do you have any questions about those risks?
