[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so on your skin, i do see some very faint erythematous papules on your cheek. it's a little bit of redness around and underneath the nostrils. your skin type is a four or five. so, let's talk a little bit about your medical history. you do have a history of rosacea, including ocular rosacea. and you've had the perioral dermatitis. and you're currently using the doxycycline cream twice a day, the metrocream, and the sulfacetamide wash, twice a day. okay, so i think we can try to go ahead and get you on the tacrolimus. i'm going to give you a prescription for that. i think that will help with the perioral dermatitis. and then i want you to continue with the sulfacetamide wash once a day. and then i want you to use the bruder mask as needed. for your rosacea, let's continue with the metrocream twice a day. and then i want you to gently wash your eyelids once a day with a gentle cleanser and try a gentle cream such as vanicream. and then we'll just check back in four weeks. does that sound good?
[patient] that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, so call if you have any problems. and i'll see you in four weeks.
