dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, mr. johnson. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i've been having some shortness of breath and coughing up some blood.
[doctor] okay. have you been experiencing any other symptoms?
[patient] no, just shortness of breath and coughing up blood.
[doctor] okay. and how long has this been going on?
[patient] about a week.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any other symptoms such as fever, chills, or sore throat?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you had any recent travel or exposure to anyone with similar symptoms?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any recent changes in your diet or exercise?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any other symptoms such as chest pain or palpitations?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. and do you have a history of asthma or any other respiratory problems?
[patient] yes, i have asthma.
[doctor] okay. and do you have a history of diabetes or hypertension?
[patient] yes, i have diabetes and hypertension.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications for these conditions?
[patient] yes, i'm taking metformin for diabetes and norvasc for hypertension.
[doctor] okay. have you been taking your medications as prescribed?
[patient] i've been taking them, but i haven't been taking them as regularly as i should.
[doctor] okay. and do you smoke or drink alcohol?
[patient] no, i don't smoke or drink alcohol.
[doctor] okay. and do you exercise regularly?
[patient] i try to exercise, but i'm not as active as i should be.
[doctor] okay. and do you have a family history of any medical conditions?
[patient] no, nothing that i know of.
[doctor] okay. well, let's do a physical exam. your blood pressure is 120/70 and your oxygen saturation is 94 percent. your heart rate is regular and you do have a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur, which is unchanged from before. your lungs are clear to auscultation, but you do have some rales and rhonchi on the right and some diminished breath sounds as well. your abdomen is soft. your lower extremities have 1+ nonpitting edema, but no calf tenderness or homan's sign.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm going to order a chest x-ray, a ct scan, and some blood work to be done in the er. i'd like you to go into the er immediately after this appointment and i will call ahead.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'd like to continue the metformin, but increase it to 750 mg twice daily. i'd also like to discontinue the norvasc. and i'd like to see you back in about 3 weeks to just discuss your diabetes and further treatment recommendations.
[patient] okay. what about my asthma?
[doctor] i'm going to continue you on your current asthma medication. but i want to see you back in 3 weeks to check on your shortness of breath and coughing up blood.
[patient] okay. sounds good. thanks.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
