dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, miss. how are you feeling today?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm just a little worried about my heart.
[doctor] okay, well, i'm glad you came in. so, tell me a little bit about your heart. have you had any chest pain?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. have you had any shortness of breath?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. have you had any leg swelling?
[patient] yeah, a little bit.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, you had a heart attack a while back, correct?
[patient] yeah, i did.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing now? are you doing any exercises?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. well, let's take a look at your heart. (pause) okay. so, your heart sounds good. you have a 3/6 systolic ejection murmur at the left base, but that's probably due to the fact that you had a heart attack. and your lungs are clear. your neck is okay. and your radial artery cath site looks good. no hematoma. and your radial pulses are palpable. and you do have some bilateral lower limb edema. pitting 1+.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na review your results. your ecg is normal. your rhythm is normal. your heart rate is good. your blood pressure is well controlled. your ejection fraction is 35 %, which is a little lower than i would like, but we'll work on that.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and your labs look good. and your blood sugar is stable. so, i'm gon na talk to you about some of the problems that you have. you have coronary artery disease, and we're gon na continue to monitor that. and you're doing a good job with your aspirin and your brilinta. i think you should continue that. and you're doing good with your lipitor and your toprol. you're doing well with your lisinopril.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm gon na add some lasix to help with your fluid. and i'm gon na add some aldactone to help with your blood pressure. and i want to do a repeat echo in about two months.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm gon na refer you to cardiac rehab for some education and to get you exercising regularly.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and then you have a type 2 diabetes, and that's stable. so, we're just gon na continue with your metformin.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and then you have hypertension, and your blood pressure is well controlled. so, we'll continue with the lisinopril. and i'm gon na give you a referral to nutrition counseling to think about some other diet options. have you thought about that?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk a little bit about that. there are some healthier alternatives to some of the preserved meats that you consume.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. well, do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll give you a referral for nutrition counseling. and then i'll give you a referral to cardiac rehab. and then i'll give you a prescription for the lasix and the aldactone. and then i'll order some labs and we'll follow up in a couple of months.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
