dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, i'm still trying to get used to this new medication and the whole thing.
[doctor] okay, so i know it's been a little bit of a transition. so, you know, you had a heart attack about six months ago, and you've been doing pretty well since then. so, tell me a little bit about how you're doing.
[patient] yeah, i'm doing okay. i'm still trying to get used to the new medication and, you know, the whole thing. i mean, it's just been a big change.
[doctor] okay. yeah, i can imagine. so, you know, we've talked about the importance of taking your medications regularly, and i know that you've been doing that. so, are you taking the aspirin and the brilinta and the fish oil and the crestor and the metoprolol?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with that? are you having any issues with any of those?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. great. and are you doing any kind of exercise? i know we talked about getting you into cardiac rehab. are you doing anything?
[patient] yeah, i'm trying to get into cardiac rehab. i'm just waiting for my doctor to get back to me with a referral.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, we've also talked about the importance of diet and exercise. are you eating well? are you watching what you're eating?
[patient] i'm trying.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood sugar? you know, we've talked about your diabetes. how's that going?
[patient] it's been a little bit of a struggle. i've been trying to get my hemoglobin a1c down.
[doctor] okay. well, we can work on that. so, tell me a little bit about what's going on with your blood sugar. are you taking insulin?
[patient] i am.
[doctor] okay. and how's that going? are you taking it once a day?
[patient] it's been a little bit of a struggle. i've been trying to get my hemoglobin a1c down.
[doctor] okay. well, we can work on that. so, you know, we're going to order another hemoglobin a1c today, and we'll get that checked. and then we'll also get you set up with a dietitian to help you with your diet and your diabetes.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i know you're taking a lot of medications. are you having any issues with those? are you having any side effects?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. great. and are you having any other symptoms? you know, are you having any chest pain or shortness of breath on exertion?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and are you feeling dizzy when you stand up quickly?
[patient] yeah, i do.
[doctor] okay. well, that's pretty common. that's just your body adjusting to the new medication. but we can work on that. so, you know, i know you're taking the metoprolol. that's a beta blocker, and that can cause some dizziness. so, we can look at that.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, we've also talked about the importance of following up with your nephrologist. are you doing that?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. great. and how's that going? are you following up with them?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. great. and are you taking your blood pressure medication?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. great. so, you know, we're going to check your blood pressure today, and we'll make sure that that's okay. and then we'll also get you set up with a cardiologist to check on your heart.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, i know you've had a heart attack, and you've had some coronary artery disease. are you having any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. great. and are you feeling depressed?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. well, we can work on that. so, you know, we're going to get you set up with a psychiatrist to help you with that. and then we'll also get you set up with some therapy to help you with that.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, we're going to go ahead and order some labs today. we're going to check your hemoglobin a1c and your creatinine level. and then we'll get you set up with a dietitian and a cardiologist and a nephrologist. and then we'll also get you set up with a psychiatrist and a therapist.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and then we'll also get you set up with a referral for cardiac rehab. so, you know, that will be really good for you. it will help you get back into shape and get you feeling better.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and then we'll also get you set up with a refill on your metoprolol and your crestor. so, you know, we'll get you all set up with everything you need.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, we'll go ahead and get you all set up with everything you need. and then we'll follow up with you in about six months to check on you.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and then we'll also get you set up with a follow-up appointment with your nephrologist.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, you know, it was good seeing you today. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. well, we'll talk to you soon. }}<|eot_id|>
