dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. taylor. how are you today?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i'm just feeling a little bit of pain in my stomach.
[doctor] mm-hmm. okay. let's talk a little bit about your medical history. you have a history of diabetes type 2, asthma, and gastritis. is that correct?
[patient] yeah, that's correct.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical conditions that i should know about?
[patient] i'm not aware of anything else.
[doctor] okay. and what about your lifestyle, ms. taylor? do you smoke or drink?
[patient] i do drink, but i don't drink a lot. i mean, i like to have a drink or two, but i'm not a heavy drinker.
[doctor] okay. and do you smoke?
[patient] no, i don't smoke.
[doctor] okay. and do you drink a lot of coffee or caffeine?
[patient] yeah, i do like my coffee. i have a cup in the morning and then i have another one in the afternoon.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other habits that you'd like to share with me?
[patient] not that i can think of.
[doctor] okay. well, let's talk a little bit about your medications. you're taking metformin 500 milligrams twice a day, is that correct?
[patient] yeah, that's correct.
[doctor] okay. and you're also taking flovent twice a day?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and do you use the albuterol as needed?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and have you had to use the albuterol recently?
[patient] no, i haven't had to use it.
[doctor] okay. good. now, let's talk a little bit about your symptoms. you mentioned that you have some abdominal pain. can you tell me more about that?
[patient] yeah, i just have this pain in my stomach. it's been going on for a few days now. it's kind of like a dull ache.
[doctor] okay. have you had any nausea or vomiting?
[patient] yeah, i have had some nausea and vomiting.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any diarrhea?
[patient] no, i haven't had any diarrhea.
[doctor] okay. and when did this start?
[patient] it started a few days ago.
[doctor] okay. and is the pain constant or does it come and go?
[patient] it's kind of constant.
[doctor] okay. and is it better or worse at any time of day?
[patient] it's about the same.
[doctor] okay. good. now, let's do a quick physical exam. i'm going to listen to your lungs. (auscultation of lungs) okay, i hear some wheezes in your lungs. i'm also going to listen to your heart. (auscultation of heart) i hear a systolic ejection murmur. it's a three out of six. and i'm going to examine your abdomen. (examination of abdomen) okay, i do appreciate some tenderness in your epigastrium. your abdomen is soft, but i don't feel any tenderness in your right lower quadrant or right upper quadrant.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm also going to check your vital signs. (takes vital signs) okay, your blood pressure is 128 over 72, your heart rate is 78, and your oxygen saturation is 98 percent on room air.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] now, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. for your abdominal pain, i think you have some gastritis, which is inflammation of the stomach lining. it's probably related to your increased caffeine intake. you do have a history of moderately heavy alcohol use, and i think that may also be a factor. i'm going to recommend that you reduce your caffeine intake and reduce your alcohol intake. i'm also going to prescribe you some zantac, which is a medication that will help with the inflammation. and i'm also going to order some blood work to check your liver enzymes and some other tests to rule out any other causes of the pain.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] for your diabetes type 2, you're doing well. i'm going to increase your metformin to 1000 milligrams in the morning and 500 milligrams at night. i want you to continue with your home blood sugar monitoring and bring those readings to your next appointment.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and for your asthma, you're doing well. i want you to continue with your flovent twice a day, even though you haven't had any recent asthma attacks. this will help prevent any future attacks. you can also use your albuterol as needed.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] now, let's talk a little bit about follow-up. i want you to come back in four weeks. i want to see how you're doing with your gastritis and i want to check on your diabetes and your asthma.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i think that's all for today. do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll see you in four weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
