dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing alright. i've had a pretty rough week.
[doctor] yeah? what's been going on?
[patient] my son, he's been playing lacrosse and he hit me in the elbow with the stick. and it's been bothering me a lot. i've been having a lot of pain and swelling.
[doctor] okay. well, let's take a look. so i'm going to go ahead and do a physical exam on you. so i'm gon na listen to your heart and lungs. and i'm gon na check your blood pressure. and i'm gon na check your abdomen and your back. and i'm gon na do a quick exam of your right elbow. so your blood pressure is 150 over 90, which is a little high. but that's not uncommon. your heart and lungs sound good. your abdomen is normal. and your back is normal. so let's take a look at your elbow. so i'm gon na go ahead and do some palpation of your olecranon area of your posterior elbow. and you do have some pain with that. you do have some pain with flexion and extension, but otherwise normal range of motion. and you do have some swelling and some ecchymosis about the elbow.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, you know, i'm gon na go ahead and order some x-rays of your elbow. and we'll see if there's any bony abnormalities. but i think based on the exam, i think you've got an elbow contusion. so i'm gon na prescribe you some ibuprofen 800 milligrams twice a day. and i want you to ice the area for 20 minutes, three times a day to help with some of the pain and swelling. and i'm gon na encourage you to avoid playing lacrosse for a couple of weeks, just until your elbow heals. after that, you should be fine to continue playing normally.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay? and i know you've got a history of high blood pressure. and i know you're on lisinopril 20 milligrams a day. and that seems to be well controlled. so i'm gon na encourage you to keep up with that. and i'm gon na order a hemoglobin a1c to check your blood sugar levels and see if you need any adjustments with your diabetes medication. you're currently on metformin 500 milligrams a day. and that seems to be well controlled. so we'll keep you on that. and i'll also go ahead and order an x-ray of your elbow. and we'll take a look at that. and if there's anything else i can do for you, just let me know. okay?
[patient] okay, that sounds good. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
