[patient] i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm gon na go ahead and order that. so, i'm gon na do a physical exam on you. so, i'm gon na listen to your heart. i don't hear any murmurs. i'm gon na listen to your lungs. your lungs sound clear. i'm gon na listen to your abdomen. your abdomen is soft. i don't feel any masses or tenderness. i'm gon na check your ankles. you have a little bit of swelling in your ankles. i'm gon na check your neck. i don't see any swelling or carotid bruits. and i'm gon na check your heart rate and rhythm. it's normal. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order some tests. i'm gon na order an ekg. i'm gon na order a hemoglobin a1c. and i'm gon na order a repeat blood pressure check. and i'm gon na have you start taking baby aspirin at 81 milligrams a day. i'm gon na have you take nitroglycerin up to three tablets every five minutes as needed. and i'm gon na have you follow up with cardiology for further evaluation. so, i think you're doing well with your diabetes, but i do think we need to watch your blood pressure. and i'm gon na have you start a hydrochlorothiazide at a low dose. and i want you to monitor your blood pressures at home over the next two weeks and report them to me via my chart. this will help us determine if any adjustments need to be made to your new medications. so, do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. and do you understand the plan?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. great. i'll have my nurse come in and we'll get you all checked out. }}<|eot_id|>
