dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, sophia. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, i guess. i've just been having some knee pain.
[doctor] okay. so, what's going on with your knee pain? have you hurt your knee or something?
[patient] no, i don't think so. it just started like six months ago.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any swelling or redness in your knee?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt all the time or just when you're doing certain things?
[patient] it hurts all the time. i have a deep achy pain. it's on the back of my patella.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any creaking in your knee?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you're sitting or standing?
[patient] when i get up from sitting.
[doctor] okay. and when you're walking up or down stairs?
[patient] yes, that hurts too.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you're running?
[patient] no, i can't run. i used to run five to six miles a day, but i can't do that anymore.
[doctor] okay. and what does it feel like when you're running?
[patient] it feels like my knee is going to give out.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing for the pain?
[patient] i've been icing it and wrapping it with an ace bandage.
[doctor] okay. and have you taken any ibuprofen or anything for the pain?
[patient] yes, i've taken ibuprofen and aleve.
[doctor] okay. and have you ever had any injuries to your knees before?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. and do you work from home?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and do you do anything that might be contributing to the pain?
[patient] i try to be as active as i can.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of activities do you do?
[patient] i like to run outdoors.
[doctor] okay. and do you do anything else?
[patient] no, just running.
[doctor] okay. so, let's take a look at your knee. i'm gon na have you hop up on the table. i'm gon na do a quick exam. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na push on your knee here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your other knee. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your foot here. does that hurt?
[patient] no, it doesn't.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your other foot. does that hurt?
[patient] no, it doesn't.
[doctor] okay. so, let's take a look at your lower extremities. i'm gon na have you stand up. i'm gon na walk you through this. i'm gon na push on your knee here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your other knee. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your foot here. does that hurt?
[patient] no, it doesn't.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na push on your other foot. does that hurt?
[patient] no, it doesn't.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na check your reflexes. i'm gon na tap on your knee here. do you feel that?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na tap on your other knee. do you feel that?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. so, let's take a look at your x-rays. everything looks good. i don't see any fractures or osteoarthritis. i think you have patellofemoral pain syndrome.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, patellofemoral pain syndrome is a condition where the pain is in the front of the knee. it's where the patella or kneecap rubs on the femur or thigh bone. and it's a very common condition. it's more common in people who are runners or people who are very active.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, the first thing i'm gon na have you do is i'm gon na have you start taking it easy for a while. i don't want you to run for now. i want you to take it easy and let the knee heal. and i'm gon na have you start doing some physical therapy to strengthen your lower extremities and to correct any incorrect running mechanics. does that sound good?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i want you to continue taking ibuprofen or anti-inflammatories as needed for the pain. does that sound good?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and i want you to follow up with me soon. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. all right. i'll see you soon.
[patient] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
